WEBVTT

00:00:14.013 --> 00:00:20.853
"CODE GEASS
Lelouch of the Rebellion I -Initiation-"

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:38.996
Announcing Prince Lelouch vi Britannia,

00:00:39.205 --> 00:00:42.792
17th heir to the Royal
Britannian Imperial throne!

00:00:44.126 --> 00:00:47.755
| heard Empress Marianne was
killed inside of the Britannian palace.

00:00:47.964 --> 00:00:51.926
There's no way terrorists
could have just gotten in there!

00:00:52.134 --> 00:00:53.553
Then, the real killers must have been...

00:00:53.761 --> 00:00:57.390
Beware, my friend! Best not to even speculate.

00:00:57.598 --> 00:01:01.519
And yet he seems so steadfast,
even though his mother is dead!

00:01:01.727 --> 00:01:04.063
But he has no path to the throne now.

00:01:04.272 --> 00:01:07.275
And the Ashford family
who backed them is finished, too.

00:01:07.483 --> 00:01:08.651
And his sister, the princess?

00:01:08.859 --> 00:01:10.152
| heard she was shot in the legs.

00:01:10.361 --> 00:01:11.696
And that she'd lost her sight.

00:01:11.904 --> 00:01:13.656
Hysterical blindness, though, right?

00:01:13.864 --> 00:01:17.535
It's the same thing. She can't even
be married off for political gain now.

00:01:17.743 --> 00:01:20.621
Your Majesty! My mother has passed away!

00:01:20.830 --> 00:01:22.331
What of it?

00:01:22.540 --> 00:01:23.082
"What of it"?!

00:01:23.291 --> 00:01:28.671
You sought an audience with the
emperor of Britannia simply to tell me that?

00:01:28.879 --> 00:01:31.757
Send in the next person!
| have no time to babysit a child!

00:01:31.966 --> 00:01:33.467
Father!

00:01:34.844 --> 00:01:36.262
Yes, Your Majesty!

00:01:36.470 --> 00:01:38.639
Why didn't you protect Mother?!

00:01:38.848 --> 00:01:41.767
You're the emperor!
The greatest man in this nation!

00:01:41.976 --> 00:01:44.061
And you haven't even visited Nunnally!

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:46.314
| have no use for weaklings!

00:01:46.522 --> 00:01:47.773
Weaklings?!

00:01:47.982 --> 00:01:50.693
That is what it means to be royalty!

00:01:53.070 --> 00:01:56.115
Then I don't want to be your heir!

00:01:56.324 --> 00:02:00.328
I've had enough being a successor
and of getting caught up in all the fighting!

00:02:00.536 --> 00:02:02.330
You are dead.

00:02:02.538 --> 00:02:06.375
What have you ever risked your life to attain?

00:02:06.584 --> 00:02:11.130
Your clothes? Your home?
Your food? Your right to succession?

00:02:11.339 --> 00:02:13.215
Nay, I gave you all these things!

00:02:13.424 --> 00:02:17.178
In short, you do not qualify as alive!

00:02:17.386 --> 00:02:19.764
Lelouch!

00:02:19.972 --> 00:02:22.183
As you are dead, you have no rights.

00:02:22.391 --> 00:02:24.560
| am sending you and Nunnally to Japan.

00:02:24.769 --> 00:02:28.814
As prince and princess,
you will serve as bargaining chips.

00:02:29.023 --> 00:02:33.069
| believe their Prime Minister's
son is your age.

00:02:33.277 --> 00:02:35.112
Inveigle him, Lelouch!

00:02:35.321 --> 00:02:38.074
You are responsible for what
only a royal can accomplish.

00:02:38.282 --> 00:02:42.703
You and Nunnally shall become
cornerstones of the Holy Britannian Empire!

00:02:42.912 --> 00:02:49.251
Know this: if you fail, there shall
be no place for you in this world!

00:02:55.883 --> 00:02:59.845
In 2009 a.t.b., the Holy Britannian Empire
sent Lelouch and Nunnally vi Britannia

00:02:59.845 --> 00:03:01.847
"Kururugi Shrine" In 2009 a.t.b., the Holy Britannian
Empire sent Lelouch and Nunnally vi Britannia

00:03:01.847 --> 00:03:04.767
In 2009 a.t.b., the Holy Britannian Empire
sent Lelouch and Nunnally vi Britannia

00:03:04.975 --> 00:03:09.814
to stay with Japan's Prime Minister Genbu
Kururugi, ostensibly as "students"” there.

00:03:10.022 --> 00:03:12.358
It was a polite term for "hostages."

00:03:34.130 --> 00:03:37.007
The island nation in the Far East
which declared its neutrality...

00:03:37.216 --> 00:03:40.428
...and Britannia,
the world's greatest superpower.

00:03:40.636 --> 00:03:43.764
There was a dispute between them
over Japan's underground resources,

00:03:43.973 --> 00:03:46.892
and the diplomatic tensions
between them were deep-rooted.

00:03:49.145 --> 00:03:54.984
Many Japanese thought that with the prince
and princess there, war could be avoided.

00:03:55.192 --> 00:03:57.403
These hopes were summarily betrayed.

00:04:00.239 --> 00:04:02.616
In the deciding battle for the mainland,

00:04:02.825 --> 00:04:05.953
the Britannian forces introduced the
humanoid autonomous battle armored knight

00:04:06.162 --> 00:04:08.122
known as the "Knightmare Frame"
into actual combat.

00:04:08.330 --> 00:04:10.583
As their power was far greater than anticipated,

00:04:10.791 --> 00:04:13.127
the mainland defensive
line of the Japanese forces

00:04:13.335 --> 00:04:16.630
was completely broken by the Knightmares.

00:04:17.631 --> 00:04:19.800
Japan became a dominion of the empire.

00:04:20.009 --> 00:04:25.264
It was stripped of its freedom,
its rights, and even its name.

00:04:25.473 --> 00:04:27.016
Area 11.

00:04:27.224 --> 00:04:32.563
That number became the new name
of the defeated nation of Japan.

00:04:36.609 --> 00:04:38.277
| swear...

00:04:38.486 --> 00:04:40.946
Suzaku, I swear...

00:04:50.456 --> 00:04:54.210
The moment when I might be able

00:04:54.418 --> 00:04:59.590
To change myself and even the world

00:04:59.799 --> 00:05:03.969
It's always right there at my side

00:05:05.596 --> 00:05:12.520
I stood still, looking at myself

00:05:12.728 --> 00:05:18.943
With undisguised frustration

00:05:19.151 --> 00:05:22.446
It's fine to feel lost, feel anguished

00:05:22.655 --> 00:05:25.991
Feel mournful as I decide what to do

00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:29.537
All it took was a single word from you

00:05:29.745 --> 00:05:33.290
And my uncertainty vanished

00:05:33.499 --> 00:05:39.672
You let the light shine into
what was my empty room

00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:43.175
The sky I had been looking up at

00:05:43.384 --> 00:05:47.137
Cleared and turned blue

00:05:47.346 --> 00:05:50.641
And I decided to throw open

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:53.727
The windows that were kept closed

00:05:53.936 --> 00:05:57.857
The moment when I might be able

00:05:58.065 --> 00:06:03.070
To change myself and even the world

00:06:03.279 --> 00:06:07.616
| feel it right here with me

00:06:12.580 --> 00:06:17.751
"7 Years After the War (2017 a.t.b.)"

00:06:17.960 --> 00:06:22.673
"Britannian Residential Zone -
Tokyo Settlement”

00:06:23.507 --> 00:06:29.388
This is alpha-3! Target is moving from delta-12
to delta-14! Moving at a speed of 80 kph!

00:06:29.597 --> 00:06:30.848
CCP to all mobile units!

00:06:31.056 --> 00:06:33.392
Declaring a code 3 from floor 5 through floor 2.

00:06:33.601 --> 00:06:36.937
Apply 2.8 to all movements
and bring in the target intact.

00:06:37.146 --> 00:06:40.649
This is footage of the recent
terrorist bombing in Osaka.

00:06:40.858 --> 00:06:43.360
Although two groups have
claimed responsibility for the attack,

00:06:43.569 --> 00:06:46.989
the Japan Liberation Front
and Blood of the Samurai--

00:06:47.197 --> 00:06:48.908
You're out of time.

00:06:49.116 --> 00:06:52.536
From here on, I'd like it to
be one move every 20 seconds.

00:06:52.745 --> 00:06:54.830
You heard him.

00:06:57.625 --> 00:07:01.045
Hm? Has your substitute arrived?

00:07:02.254 --> 00:07:06.550
I'm saved! But shouldn't you be at school?

00:07:06.759 --> 00:07:10.054
Aw, just students?

00:07:10.262 --> 00:07:12.848
Aw, just a nobleman?

00:07:13.057 --> 00:07:15.976
| envy the young.
They have so much time on their hands.

00:07:16.185 --> 00:07:19.271
So much time for regrets... Your name?

00:07:19.480 --> 00:07:21.732
Lelouch Lamperouge.

00:07:21.941 --> 00:07:26.111
Whoa! Whoa! You can't win this,
no matter what you do, right?

00:07:26.320 --> 00:07:30.866
Rivalz, in how many minutes should
we leave here in order to make our next class?

00:07:31.075 --> 00:07:33.285
Um, if we really haul ass, about 20 minutes.

00:07:33.494 --> 00:07:37.498
In that case, I'll ask you
to drive safely on the way back.

00:07:37.706 --> 00:07:40.668
I'll need nine minutes.
Owner, about yesterday's matter...

00:07:40.876 --> 00:07:42.962
Understood. I'll arrange it.

00:07:43.170 --> 00:07:47.633
Nine minutes? You have 20 seconds per move.

00:07:47.841 --> 00:07:49.510
More than enough.

00:07:49.718 --> 00:07:51.804
You're starting with the king?

00:07:56.266 --> 00:07:58.769
Goddammit! After we finally steal this thing!

00:07:58.978 --> 00:08:02.439
It's all because Tamaki
couldn't stick to Naoto's plan!

00:08:04.733 --> 00:08:06.527
| love playing nobility!

00:08:06.735 --> 00:08:09.321
Their pride ensures that
they pay what they owe you.

00:08:09.530 --> 00:08:11.991
Besides that, eight minutes,
32 seconds is a new record!

00:08:12.199 --> 00:08:14.118
Nobility make such tepid opponents.

00:08:14.326 --> 00:08:16.036
They're just parasites
living off their privilege.

00:08:16.245 --> 00:08:20.624
So, why not try one of the Elevens?
Unlike like us Britannians, they--

00:08:20.833 --> 00:08:21.875
It's just cruel.

00:08:22.084 --> 00:08:23.627
These Elevens scare me!

00:08:26.338 --> 00:08:27.464
We now bring you an address

00:08:27.673 --> 00:08:31.844
by His Royal Highness Prince Clovis,
third prince of the Britannian Empire.

00:08:33.554 --> 00:08:36.098
To my imperial subjects!

00:08:36.306 --> 00:08:40.936
And of course, to the many
Elevens who cooperate with us!

00:08:41.145 --> 00:08:43.105
We're not Elevens! We're Japanese!

00:08:43.313 --> 00:08:48.110
Do you see? Right now,
my heart is torn in half!

00:08:48.318 --> 00:08:51.071
Into a heart filled with sadness
and a heart filled with rage!

00:08:51.280 --> 00:08:56.869
However, as ruler of Area 11,
| must never be daunted by terrorism!

00:08:57.077 --> 00:08:59.747
The reason being that the battle
we fight is a righteous one!

00:08:59.955 --> 00:09:01.957
A righteous battle
to protect the happiness of--

00:09:03.042 --> 00:09:04.835
That first move you made...

00:09:05.044 --> 00:09:07.254
Why'd you start with the king?

00:09:07.463 --> 00:09:11.258
If the king doesn't lead, how can
he expect his subordinates to follow?

00:09:11.467 --> 00:09:12.426
About that...

00:09:12.634 --> 00:09:13.260
What?

00:09:13.469 --> 00:09:16.847
Do you want to run a
corporation or something?

00:09:17.848 --> 00:09:19.892
No way.

00:09:20.100 --> 00:09:22.269
Whoa! What the hell?!

00:09:22.478 --> 00:09:24.271
Pay attention to the road, you jerks!

00:09:24.480 --> 00:09:26.356
Stop! Not that way!

00:09:32.988 --> 00:09:36.533
Um... Was that our fault?

00:09:36.742 --> 00:09:39.536
Control, the target has crashed at the
abandoned V.O. building construction site.

00:09:39.745 --> 00:09:43.749
Hold it. The military's taking this over.
General Bartley is in command.

00:09:43.957 --> 00:09:45.542
The general?!

00:09:45.751 --> 00:09:50.089
We have to retrieve it,
no matter what. That thing is...!

00:09:51.340 --> 00:09:52.174
What's that?

00:09:52.382 --> 00:09:55.928
Hey, Lelouch! It looks like
our energy line's been cut.

00:09:56.136 --> 00:09:57.763
Right... Say, what's that--

00:09:57.971 --> 00:10:00.099
Hey! Over here!

00:10:00.766 --> 00:10:01.391
Nasty.

00:10:01.600 --> 00:10:02.768
What, was there some sort of accident?

00:10:02.976 --> 00:10:04.228
Probably a drunk driver.

00:10:04.436 --> 00:10:05.395
That idiot!

00:10:05.604 --> 00:10:08.232
Hey, someone should go help them!

00:10:09.817 --> 00:10:11.527
All these fools!

00:10:12.903 --> 00:10:14.780
Hey! Wait!

00:10:18.784 --> 00:10:20.953
Look! The student rescue team has arrived!

00:10:21.161 --> 00:10:23.247
Would somebody at least call the police?

00:10:23.455 --> 00:10:25.457
Hey! Are you all right?!

00:10:27.793 --> 00:10:28.794
Seriously, man...

00:10:29.002 --> 00:10:32.631
| wish you'd stop demonstrating
this pointless pride of yours.

00:10:32.840 --> 00:10:35.217
We're gonna be late for class now!

00:10:36.718 --> 00:10:38.387
Nagata? Nagata!

00:10:39.555 --> 00:10:41.807
Hey! Can you hear me in there?!

00:10:42.015 --> 00:10:44.726
I've found you. My...

00:10:46.353 --> 00:10:47.896
Where?

00:10:49.189 --> 00:10:50.941
Are you in there?

00:10:54.361 --> 00:10:56.780
Hey! Stop! I'm not--

00:10:57.364 --> 00:11:00.284
Could something like
that be called a hit and run?

00:11:01.702 --> 00:11:03.328
Why don't they have a ladder on the inside?!

00:11:03.537 --> 00:11:05.330
Warning!

00:11:05.539 --> 00:11:08.500
Surrender now and you still have
a chance to defend yourself in court.

00:11:08.709 --> 00:11:11.128
Halt at once.

00:11:11.336 --> 00:11:13.422
The next rounds will hit you. Halt at once.

00:11:13.630 --> 00:11:15.841
They've called in the army! Now what?!

00:11:16.049 --> 00:11:18.385
That's why I'm here, isn't it?!

00:11:20.387 --> 00:11:23.473
It'd be dangerous to get out.
Sounds like there's trouble out there.

00:11:23.682 --> 00:11:25.225
I'll use my phone...

00:11:27.603 --> 00:11:29.646
Can you enter the
subway via the Azabu route?

00:11:29.855 --> 00:11:31.899
Kallen! Let's use it here!

00:11:32.107 --> 00:11:33.692
That'd mean a slaughter!

00:11:33.901 --> 00:11:36.445
Yeah, you're right...

00:11:36.653 --> 00:11:38.197
That woman...

00:11:39.239 --> 00:11:42.492
Where are you, Lelouch?
We've gotta get to school!

00:11:42.701 --> 00:11:44.745
The target's moving from
the settlement area to the ghetto.

00:11:44.953 --> 00:11:45.829
Good. Corner them!

00:11:46.038 --> 00:11:47.539
Yes, my lord.

00:11:50.334 --> 00:11:52.252
A slash harken?!

00:11:53.962 --> 00:11:55.464
A Knightmare!

00:11:58.800 --> 00:12:00.928
Shit! These guys are actual terrorists!

00:12:01.136 --> 00:12:04.223
You guys know full well
how powerful this thing is!

00:12:07.768 --> 00:12:10.896
The rest of you, back off. I'll take this guy.

00:12:11.897 --> 00:12:14.441
| don't know where you got that thing,

00:12:14.650 --> 00:12:19.363
but an old Glasgow will never
be able to stop this Sutherland.

00:12:19.571 --> 00:12:21.448
Much less one piloted by a damned Eleven

00:12:21.657 --> 00:12:24.284
who can't appreciate our Emperor's affection!

00:12:26.078 --> 00:12:27.579
Kallen, we need to split up!

00:12:27.788 --> 00:12:29.623
We can't both get killed! Run for it!

00:12:29.831 --> 00:12:30.999
But...!

00:12:37.172 --> 00:12:39.132
How simpleminded.

00:12:40.425 --> 00:12:42.010
What's wrong?! Dammit!

00:12:42.219 --> 00:12:44.012
Secondhand junk!

00:12:47.641 --> 00:12:48.308
Oh ho!

00:12:48.517 --> 00:12:51.770
| like your spirit. However!

00:12:53.105 --> 00:12:54.898
I'm outside my phone's range.

00:12:55.107 --> 00:12:56.900
This darkness and the road surface...

00:12:57.109 --> 00:12:59.361
We must be speeding
along the old subway lines.

00:12:59.569 --> 00:13:02.114
They're headed for a ghetto somewhere.

00:13:02.322 --> 00:13:04.199
Okay, I've got it.

00:13:04.408 --> 00:13:05.701
The conditions have been cleared.

00:13:05.909 --> 00:13:08.787
| may not like army protection much,
but if I give them a terrorist communicator...

00:13:08.787 --> 00:13:10.122
"Shinjuku Imperial Gardens" | may not like army protection
much, but if I give them a terrorist communicator...

00:13:10.122 --> 00:13:11.665
"Shinjuku Imperial Gardens"

00:13:11.665 --> 00:13:12.958
Ah-ha!

00:13:13.166 --> 00:13:14.293
Wh-Why do you know about it?!

00:13:14.501 --> 00:13:16.086
Our guess was right, then?

00:13:16.295 --> 00:13:17.337
Why, you!

00:13:17.546 --> 00:13:19.131
You overdid it.

00:13:19.339 --> 00:13:24.219
The terrorists stole something you and
Prince Clovis were working on secretly.

00:13:24.428 --> 00:13:25.929
Retrieving it would be simple,

00:13:26.138 --> 00:13:28.307
but you want to sweep up
their compatriots as well.

00:13:28.515 --> 00:13:31.226
If you let the terrorists go,
you'll find their hideout, too.

00:13:31.435 --> 00:13:34.271
Congratulations!
Your reasoning was bang on target!

00:13:34.479 --> 00:13:36.815
Well, I just thought it was strange...

00:13:37.024 --> 00:13:38.108
Enough!

00:13:38.317 --> 00:13:40.235
So, what does the
Special Corps want in all this?

00:13:40.444 --> 00:13:43.155
I'm saying I'd like to help with the cleanup!

00:13:43.363 --> 00:13:44.197
"Help"?!

00:13:44.406 --> 00:13:46.408
Yes. I want data.

00:13:46.616 --> 00:13:50.329
So, what is it they stole, anyway?

00:13:51.330 --> 00:13:55.417
Chemical weapons.
In other words... Poison gas.

00:13:58.503 --> 00:14:01.340
The terrorists are hiding
inside the subway system.

00:14:01.548 --> 00:14:05.260
Your mission is to find the
weapon stolen by the terrorists.

00:14:05.469 --> 00:14:07.429
Call in as soon as you spot them.

00:14:07.637 --> 00:14:10.640
Recovery of the target will
be handled by us in the royal guard.

00:14:10.849 --> 00:14:14.686
You may be honorary Britannians now,
but you were originally Elevens!

00:14:14.895 --> 00:14:16.980
The stench of these monkeys
should be familiar to you!

00:14:17.189 --> 00:14:20.192
Here's your chance to show
your loyalty to Britannia!

00:14:20.400 --> 00:14:22.361
Yes, my lord!

00:14:33.121 --> 00:14:36.124
N-No good...

00:14:36.333 --> 00:14:39.336
Please, Ohgi... Find me!

00:14:48.512 --> 00:14:50.305
4-0-4 has sighted the target.

00:14:50.514 --> 00:14:52.432
Right. Prepare for recovery!

00:15:01.858 --> 00:15:03.985
Are you military?

00:15:04.194 --> 00:15:05.237
Enough with the killing!

00:15:05.445 --> 00:15:06.446
Wait! I'm--!

00:15:06.655 --> 00:15:08.281
| can't believe you people
would use poison gas!

00:15:08.490 --> 00:15:09.991
Don't play dumb!

00:15:10.200 --> 00:15:12.244
| said wait!

00:15:12.452 --> 00:15:16.623
If there's any poison gas here,
it was Britannia that made it, right?!

00:15:16.832 --> 00:15:18.166
You...

00:15:18.375 --> 00:15:19.876
You don't want more deaths?!

00:15:20.085 --> 00:15:22.587
Then I'll just have to obliterate Britannia!

00:15:22.796 --> 00:15:24.673
Lelouch?

00:15:24.881 --> 00:15:27.801
It's me, Suzaku.

00:15:28.009 --> 00:15:31.304
You became a Britannian soldier?

00:15:31.513 --> 00:15:33.432
And you? Don't tell me this is your--

00:15:33.640 --> 00:15:35.475
No, this is--

00:15:48.029 --> 00:15:51.116
It's... not poison gas?

00:15:57.289 --> 00:15:59.499
I'm sorry. I left my radio in the trailer...

00:15:59.708 --> 00:16:03.837
It's okay. The Glasgow's systems are usable.
Anyway, were we right?

00:16:04.045 --> 00:16:06.840
Yeah. I think it's poison gas,
like our intelligence said.

00:16:07.048 --> 00:16:07.841
And Nagata?

00:16:08.049 --> 00:16:11.261
I'm not sure where he is. I can't contact him...

00:16:14.097 --> 00:16:18.560
Answer me, Suzaku.
Does this girl look like "poison gas"?

00:16:18.768 --> 00:16:21.688
But that's what we were told in the briefing!

00:16:24.065 --> 00:16:25.734
Damn monkey!

00:16:25.942 --> 00:16:28.737
Even an honorary Britannian doesn't
have the authority to do what you've done!

00:16:28.945 --> 00:16:31.406
But I was told this was poison gas!

00:16:31.615 --> 00:16:33.867
You have no right to protest!

00:16:36.203 --> 00:16:40.165
However, in reward for your
great achievements, I'll be merciful.

00:16:40.373 --> 00:16:44.628
Private Kururugi,
use this to execute the terrorist.

00:16:44.836 --> 00:16:48.215
He's not a terrorist! He's a civilian
who got caught up in this!

00:16:48.423 --> 00:16:49.508
You little...!

00:16:49.716 --> 00:16:53.470
That's an order! Didn't you
swear your loyalty to Britannia?!

00:16:53.678 --> 00:16:56.056
Yes, but...

00:16:56.264 --> 00:16:57.933
But I can't.

00:16:58.141 --> 00:16:59.226
What?

00:16:59.434 --> 00:17:01.478
| won't do it.

00:17:01.686 --> 00:17:05.857
| won't shoot a civilian. Not him.

00:17:06.066 --> 00:17:07.484
Suzaku!

00:17:08.693 --> 00:17:12.989
You look like a Britannian student,
but it's just not your day.

00:17:13.198 --> 00:17:15.450
After you've retaken the girl, kill the student!

00:17:15.659 --> 00:17:17.911
Yes, my lord!

00:17:18.119 --> 00:17:20.789
Goddamned... Britannians...

00:17:22.874 --> 00:17:26.086
Long live Japan!

00:17:29.506 --> 00:17:32.217
They got away?!
You call yourselves the royal guard?!

00:17:32.425 --> 00:17:33.760
F-Forgive me, my lord.

00:17:33.969 --> 00:17:36.972
The blast was mainly directed
upwards, but the bedrock...

00:17:37.180 --> 00:17:39.599
Why do you think I only
told you people about this?!

00:17:39.808 --> 00:17:42.269
W-We'll continue the search!

00:17:42.477 --> 00:17:44.771
The plan has moved to the next phase.

00:17:44.980 --> 00:17:46.565
But, Your Highness!

00:17:46.773 --> 00:17:48.525
It can't be helped.

00:17:48.733 --> 00:17:54.030
If knowledge of her gets out,
| could be disinherited.

00:17:54.239 --> 00:17:57.409
As Clovis, third prince
of the empire, I order you!

00:17:57.617 --> 00:18:00.996
Destroy the Shinjuku ghetto!

00:18:06.251 --> 00:18:08.878
"CRUSH THE EMPIRE"

00:18:11.381 --> 00:18:12.549
Why are the Britannians doing this?!

00:18:12.757 --> 00:18:14.426
Dear, please!

00:18:17.178 --> 00:18:20.932
Your enemies are garbage who can
never even become honorary Britannians!

00:18:21.141 --> 00:18:24.185
Wipe out every last one of them!

00:18:24.394 --> 00:18:25.270
Naturally.

00:18:25.478 --> 00:18:29.065
Supervisor Jeremiah, General Bartley
wants you to take command of Area 2...

00:18:29.274 --> 00:18:31.067
He's got staff officers, right?

00:18:31.276 --> 00:18:34.529
It's been ages since I've had
this much fun on the front lines!

00:18:45.040 --> 00:18:47.250
What the hell are you?!

00:18:47.459 --> 00:18:51.421
This chaos is all your fault, isn't it?!

00:18:51.630 --> 00:18:53.757
And on top of that, the Britannians have...

00:18:53.965 --> 00:18:56.635
They've even killed Suzaku!

00:18:58.887 --> 00:19:00.138
Not there?

00:19:00.347 --> 00:19:01.973
It looks like he's gone to the front line.

00:19:02.182 --> 00:19:04.643
Even though we brought the Lancelot here?

00:19:04.851 --> 00:19:06.019
What should we do?

00:19:06.227 --> 00:19:09.731
Well, since we don't have a Devicer...

00:19:10.649 --> 00:19:12.776
Wait there, okay?

00:19:16.112 --> 00:19:16.780
Well?

00:19:16.988 --> 00:19:19.032
Looks like only Elevens here, sir.

00:19:19.240 --> 00:19:20.533
Hm...

00:19:20.742 --> 00:19:23.161
One of the exits is near here, isn't it?

00:19:23.370 --> 00:19:26.873
Yes, sir. It matches up
with our map of the old city.

00:19:38.093 --> 00:19:40.553
That jerk hung up on me!

00:19:43.932 --> 00:19:46.935
An appropriate location for
a terrorist to meet his end, isn't it?

00:19:47.143 --> 00:19:48.186
You people...

00:19:48.395 --> 00:19:51.022
Still, you did well for a student.

00:19:51.231 --> 00:19:53.274
That's a Britannian for you!

00:19:53.483 --> 00:19:57.028
However, your future ends right here.

00:19:58.279 --> 00:20:00.198
Don't kill him!

00:20:04.619 --> 00:20:07.122
Hey!

00:20:07.330 --> 00:20:10.250
I'd hoped to bring her
back alive if possible, but...

00:20:10.458 --> 00:20:12.585
We'll tell our superiors the following:

00:20:12.794 --> 00:20:17.298
The royal guard found the
terrorists' hideout and wiped them out.

00:20:17.507 --> 00:20:20.885
However, the hostage had
already been tortured to death.

00:20:21.094 --> 00:20:23.346
What do you think, Mr. Student?

00:20:23.555 --> 00:20:25.557
What is this?

00:20:25.765 --> 00:20:28.601
Suzaku... And now this girl...

00:20:28.810 --> 00:20:34.232
Will I end here, too?
Without having accomplished a single thing?

00:20:36.860 --> 00:20:40.572
You don't want to end here, do you?

00:20:40.780 --> 00:20:41.656
What's...?

00:20:41.865 --> 00:20:44.951
You appear to have a reason for living.

00:20:45.160 --> 00:20:47.454
The girl? It can't be!

00:20:47.662 --> 00:20:50.957
If you had power, you could live, then?

00:20:51.166 --> 00:20:52.876
I'll make a deal with you.

00:20:53.084 --> 00:20:57.964
In exchange for power, you must
make one wish of mine come true.

00:20:58.173 --> 00:21:01.885
Accept this contract, and while
you will live in the world of humans,

00:21:02.093 --> 00:21:05.513
you will live unlike any other human.

00:21:05.722 --> 00:21:10.810
A different providence,
a different time, a different life.

00:21:11.019 --> 00:21:13.980
The power of the king will isolate you.

00:21:14.189 --> 00:21:16.775
If you are prepared for that...

00:21:18.318 --> 00:21:21.946
Very well! I accept your contract!

00:21:27.577 --> 00:21:34.709
Tell me, how should a Britannian
who hates Britannia live?

00:21:34.918 --> 00:21:37.921
Ah, are you an anti-nationalist?

00:21:38.129 --> 00:21:42.300
What's wrong? Why not shoot?
Your opponent is just a student.

00:21:42.509 --> 00:21:44.260
Or have you realized?

00:21:44.469 --> 00:21:48.473
The only people who should kill
are those prepared to die themselves!

00:21:49.808 --> 00:21:51.851
Wh-What's this?

00:21:52.060 --> 00:21:54.354
Lelouch vi Britannia orders you!

00:21:54.562 --> 00:21:57.816
All of you... Die!

00:22:08.409 --> 00:22:10.245
Yes, Your Highness!

00:22:25.510 --> 00:22:27.053
Thank you.

00:22:42.944 --> 00:22:45.154
Why are the royal guard all...?!

00:22:48.741 --> 00:22:52.912
What happened? What's a
Britannian student doing here?!

00:22:53.121 --> 00:22:54.539
Answer me!

00:22:56.457 --> 00:22:58.668
Answer me!

00:22:58.877 --> 00:23:02.630
Come out of there. At once!

00:23:02.839 --> 00:23:06.426
Who do you think you are?

00:23:06.634 --> 00:23:10.889
| see. It doesn't work
unless they see it directly.

00:23:11.097 --> 00:23:13.808
My name is Alan Spacer.
My father is a marquess.

00:23:14.017 --> 00:23:15.393
A marquess's son?

00:23:15.602 --> 00:23:17.812
My I.D. card's in my breast pocket.

00:23:18.021 --> 00:23:20.607
After you confirm my identity,
| ask for your protection.

00:23:27.363 --> 00:23:30.700
Keep your hands up. I'll take out your I.D.

00:23:30.909 --> 00:23:33.995
Now hand over your Knightmare to me.

00:23:42.754 --> 00:23:48.468
Understood. Its number is XG2-1G2D4.

00:23:48.676 --> 00:23:50.178
Good.

00:23:54.432 --> 00:23:57.185
What did I just...?

00:23:59.646 --> 00:24:02.523
Poor you!

00:24:02.732 --> 00:24:05.693
Looks like you missed your chance
to go to heaven, eh, Private Kururugi?

00:24:05.902 --> 00:24:07.528
Um...

00:24:07.737 --> 00:24:08.404
Where am I?

00:24:08.613 --> 00:24:11.115
Hm? Ah. Still in the Shinjuku ghetto.

00:24:11.324 --> 00:24:15.662
With Prince Clovis near,
it's the safest place there is.

00:24:15.870 --> 00:24:18.331
This is what protected you, Suzaku.

00:24:18.539 --> 00:24:22.126
Though all it did was prevent
a ricochet inside your protective suit.

00:24:22.335 --> 00:24:23.628
Is it something important to you?

00:24:23.836 --> 00:24:25.004
Y-Yeah...

00:24:25.213 --> 00:24:29.092
| hear that Elevens believe gods
dwell inside of objects.

00:24:29.300 --> 00:24:29.842
This type of--

00:24:30.051 --> 00:24:32.387
Um, is Lel--

00:24:32.595 --> 00:24:34.514
What's the situation?

00:24:34.722 --> 00:24:36.724
It sounds like the poison gas was released.

00:24:36.933 --> 00:24:39.268
They say there have been
massive casualties among the Elevens.

00:24:39.477 --> 00:24:41.729
They don't seem to have
found the perpetrators yet.

00:24:41.938 --> 00:24:43.731
| see. Not yet...

00:24:43.940 --> 00:24:48.653
Private Kururugi, do you have
experience piloting a Knightmare Frame?

00:24:48.861 --> 00:24:52.323
Of course not.
Native Elevens can't be knights.

00:24:52.532 --> 00:24:54.158
What if you could?

00:25:01.416 --> 00:25:02.917
Damned Britannians! How dare they!

00:25:03.126 --> 00:25:05.003
Kallen! The Glasgow can still move?!

00:25:05.211 --> 00:25:07.714
It's all right! I'll play decoy!

00:25:07.922 --> 00:25:09.966
Ohgi, you get the people here away!

00:25:10.174 --> 00:25:12.093
We have to make sure the only ones
caught are us in the resistance!

00:25:12.301 --> 00:25:15.430
| know, but they've got us surrounded!

00:25:18.516 --> 00:25:20.351
But that's because of weak leg muscles.

00:25:20.560 --> 00:25:23.021
No, no. I sink because I gained weight.

00:25:23.229 --> 00:25:24.397
Because you snack!

00:25:24.605 --> 00:25:27.150
Don't worry, I doubled
my practice time to burn calories.

00:25:27.358 --> 00:25:29.736
But you ate extra, too.

00:25:29.944 --> 00:25:33.614
Lulu? What have you been up to?
Where are you now?

00:25:33.823 --> 00:25:35.408
If you keep cutting class,
you'll get held back--

00:25:35.616 --> 00:25:36.909
Are you near a TV?

00:25:37.118 --> 00:25:38.578
ATV?

00:25:38.786 --> 00:25:40.455
Sorry. But this is important.

00:25:40.663 --> 00:25:41.622
Jeez...

00:25:41.831 --> 00:25:44.667
Hang on. Sorry, can I change the channel?

00:25:44.876 --> 00:25:45.710
Huh? What's up?

00:25:45.918 --> 00:25:47.879
The news. Is there anything about Shinjuku?

00:25:48.087 --> 00:25:50.214
The news? Let's see...

00:25:50.423 --> 00:25:53.134
Nothing on except stuff
about traffic being restricted.

00:25:53.342 --> 00:25:54.218
Why is it restricted?

00:25:54.427 --> 00:25:57.055
Dunno. They're not saying anything special.

00:25:57.263 --> 00:26:02.977
| see. They'll finish everyone off,
then just release whatever story they want to.

00:26:03.186 --> 00:26:06.272
You're gambling again, aren't you?

00:26:06.481 --> 00:26:08.733
| told you before how dangerous that is!

00:26:08.941 --> 00:26:10.610
Yeah, I know.

00:26:10.818 --> 00:26:15.907
Oh, and tell my little sister
I'm going to be late coming home. Bye.

00:26:16.115 --> 00:26:17.617
Since they're suppressing information,

00:26:17.825 --> 00:26:19.535
they can't easily call in reinforcements.

00:26:19.744 --> 00:26:22.747
In short, they have to work with
the pieces they now have on the board.

00:26:22.955 --> 00:26:27.210
Even so, surrounded like this,
it'll be difficult to break through by myself.

00:26:27.418 --> 00:26:29.796
And seeking army
protection would be dangerous.

00:26:34.425 --> 00:26:37.136
How about you pay me back
for dragging me into your fight?

00:26:40.056 --> 00:26:42.016
That Glasgow, huh?

00:26:48.481 --> 00:26:50.024
Only 30 minutes left!

00:26:50.233 --> 00:26:51.275
The west entrance!

00:26:51.484 --> 00:26:53.820
Use the train tracks to move
over to the west entrance!

00:26:54.028 --> 00:26:56.155
Who is this?! How do you know this code?!

00:26:56.364 --> 00:26:59.450
It doesn't matter who I am!
If you want to win, then trust me!

00:26:59.659 --> 00:27:01.119
Win?

00:27:05.998 --> 00:27:08.167
Hey! What do I do next?

00:27:09.210 --> 00:27:11.129
Pathetic Eleven...

00:27:11.337 --> 00:27:14.423
What kind of hunt is this if you just run away?

00:27:17.552 --> 00:27:19.804
Since you trusted me, you get to win.

00:27:20.012 --> 00:27:21.180
Jump onto the train!

00:27:21.389 --> 00:27:23.975
Gotcha.

00:27:24.183 --> 00:27:28.104
Did you really think
this silly plan would work?

00:27:28.312 --> 00:27:29.647
You go after the Glasgow.

00:27:29.856 --> 00:27:32.150
Yes, my lord.

00:27:32.358 --> 00:27:33.818
What?

00:27:36.362 --> 00:27:38.322
F-Friendly fire?!

00:27:38.531 --> 00:27:39.866
What's your unit?!

00:27:40.074 --> 00:27:41.993
The enemy is a one-armed--

00:27:42.201 --> 00:27:44.162
Can it be... A terrorist?!

00:27:47.123 --> 00:27:49.458
Y-You son of a...

00:28:01.470 --> 00:28:05.099
You saved my butt!
But how did you get a Sutherland?

00:28:05.308 --> 00:28:08.019
What? Where did he...?

00:28:08.227 --> 00:28:10.938
Hey! Kallen! What was with
that radio message before?

00:28:11.147 --> 00:28:12.940
Huh? He contacted you, too?

00:28:13.149 --> 00:28:16.819
Yeah! Yoshida's group
should be here soon, too--

00:28:17.028 --> 00:28:17.987
You're the leader?

00:28:18.196 --> 00:28:19.655
Huh? Yeah.

00:28:19.864 --> 00:28:22.533
The contents of that train are my gift to you.

00:28:22.742 --> 00:28:24.952
They're tools for your victory.

00:28:25.161 --> 00:28:28.414
If you wish to use them and win,
then follow my orders.

00:28:29.790 --> 00:28:30.708
There are more over here!

00:28:30.917 --> 00:28:31.751
Here, too!

00:28:31.959 --> 00:28:34.754
This is amazing! Let's hear what he has to say.

00:28:34.962 --> 00:28:36.005
Woman in the Glasgow!

00:28:36.214 --> 00:28:36.839
Y-Yes?

00:28:37.048 --> 00:28:40.009
Stay where you are. That unit
is suited to creating a disturbance.

00:28:40.218 --> 00:28:41.385
U-Understood...

00:28:41.594 --> 00:28:42.511
Energy filler status?

00:28:42.720 --> 00:28:43.971
| have about 15 minutes left.

00:28:44.180 --> 00:28:45.556
Then load a new one in.

00:28:45.765 --> 00:28:48.893
In 10 minutes, I'll contact you
with your next instructions.

00:28:50.895 --> 00:28:53.189
This is surprisingly exhausting.

00:28:53.397 --> 00:28:56.692
Still, I need the determination to succeed.

00:28:56.901 --> 00:29:00.446
I'm betting my life in this game, after all.

00:29:00.655 --> 00:29:02.365
Hey, are you sure about this?

00:29:02.573 --> 00:29:05.826
Their I.F.F.s are disabled.
It could be an enemy trap.

00:29:06.035 --> 00:29:08.663
The other side has the
total advantage in this war.

00:29:08.871 --> 00:29:10.665
They don't need to set any traps!

00:29:10.873 --> 00:29:12.541
You guys get to your assigned points, too.

00:29:12.750 --> 00:29:14.126
P-1, can you operate it?

00:29:14.335 --> 00:29:16.879
The fundamentals shouldn't be
different from what you're used to.

00:29:17.088 --> 00:29:19.298
Who are you? At least tell us your name.

00:29:19.507 --> 00:29:23.094
| can't do that. What if these
signals are being intercepted?

00:29:23.302 --> 00:29:26.847
Anyway, enemy Sutherlands
will be reaching you in 23 seconds.

00:29:27.056 --> 00:29:28.266
Probably two of them.

00:29:28.474 --> 00:29:30.268
Shoot them through the wall.

00:29:30.476 --> 00:29:31.852
Yeah, right!

00:29:32.061 --> 00:29:34.355
Everyone double-check your weapons.

00:29:34.563 --> 00:29:37.358
Hey! Are you serious?!

00:29:37.566 --> 00:29:39.360
Enemy spotted at point F-31.

00:29:39.568 --> 00:29:41.988
A feint? The monkeys play at being human.

00:29:42.196 --> 00:29:43.948
Have Lazlo's squad head straight in!

00:29:44.156 --> 00:29:47.952
Send in Eugen and Valerie!
Have them strike from the rear!

00:29:48.160 --> 00:29:51.872
3... 2... 1... Fire!

00:29:53.457 --> 00:29:55.334
Wh-What?!

00:29:56.794 --> 00:29:59.880
Sir Eugen and Sir Valerie, both lost!

00:30:00.089 --> 00:30:01.549
An ambush?

00:30:03.592 --> 00:30:05.761
An I.D. signal can be a double-edged sword.

00:30:05.970 --> 00:30:09.390
And if the terrorists follow my commands,

00:30:09.598 --> 00:30:11.976
then I've virtually
cleared the conditions here.

00:30:12.184 --> 00:30:13.561
P-1, P-4, P-7!

00:30:13.769 --> 00:30:16.981
Move 100 meters to the right and fire
your slash harkens towards three o'clock.

00:30:17.189 --> 00:30:19.108
All right! Do what the voice says, people!

00:30:19.317 --> 00:30:21.193
Fine, fine, okay!

00:30:21.402 --> 00:30:22.653
Aren't you moving yet, P-5?

00:30:22.862 --> 00:30:24.739
Quit calling me that!

00:30:25.614 --> 00:30:27.491
Enemies have moved to G-28!

00:30:27.700 --> 00:30:30.286
Send Lazlo's squad--
| mean, Glaube after them!

00:30:30.494 --> 00:30:34.040
Is it possible the terrorists
have gotten our forces' weaponry?!

00:30:41.839 --> 00:30:44.342
Sir Glaube has ejected! Frame has been lost!

00:30:44.550 --> 00:30:46.635
This failure is unacceptable!

00:30:46.844 --> 00:30:47.595
Forgive me--

00:30:47.803 --> 00:30:49.055
Hello there!

00:30:49.263 --> 00:30:51.015
What is it?! We're in
the middle of an operation!

00:30:51.223 --> 00:30:53.934
Well, I think we should deploy
the A.S.E.E.C.'s advanced weapon soon.

00:30:54.143 --> 00:30:55.978
This isn't the time!

00:30:57.063 --> 00:30:59.023
R-2, fire anchor.

00:31:00.483 --> 00:31:02.276
B-7, use U.N. ordnance.

00:31:03.361 --> 00:31:05.529
N-group, keep advancing.

00:31:06.947 --> 00:31:08.783
We just lost Lazlo's squad!

00:31:08.991 --> 00:31:11.285
Now! Bring up Quincy's squad!

00:31:11.494 --> 00:31:13.746
Your Highness, if we do that,
we break the encirclement!

00:31:13.954 --> 00:31:17.249
Now then, the enemy has five options.

00:31:17.458 --> 00:31:20.169
You can send my guards to close the gap.

00:31:20.378 --> 00:31:23.464
We're certain that the
enemy has his forces right here!

00:31:25.383 --> 00:31:27.218
Are we breaking formation?

00:31:27.426 --> 00:31:31.013
Well, they made the stupidest possible move.

00:31:31.222 --> 00:31:33.307
Q-1, your map is accurate, right?

00:31:33.516 --> 00:31:35.184
Right. At least for the old town...

00:31:35.393 --> 00:31:37.520
All right, send Bertz and the others in as well!

00:31:37.728 --> 00:31:38.771
Mission number 3.

00:31:38.979 --> 00:31:40.940
Surround them and
concentrate our forces there!

00:31:41.148 --> 00:31:42.108
| assume you're ready?

00:31:42.316 --> 00:31:45.069
The terrorists' main force
is where the center dot is!

00:31:45.277 --> 00:31:47.196
Finish them!

00:31:57.498 --> 00:31:59.083
What? The enemy isn't there?!

00:31:59.291 --> 00:32:01.794
With this, I call check.

00:32:13.639 --> 00:32:15.099
It worked, didn't it?!

00:32:15.307 --> 00:32:16.809
| can do it! I can!

00:32:17.017 --> 00:32:19.437
| can defeat Britannia!

00:32:20.896 --> 00:32:25.025
Who... Who in God's name am I fighting?!

00:32:25.234 --> 00:32:26.193
Lloyd!

00:32:26.402 --> 00:32:27.319
Yes?

00:32:27.528 --> 00:32:30.531
Can it win? Will your toy beat them?

00:32:30.739 --> 00:32:34.952
Your Highness... Please call it Lancelot.

00:32:35.161 --> 00:32:38.747
Advanced weapon
Z-0-1 Lancelot, now activating.

00:32:38.956 --> 00:32:41.083
Lancelot, activating.

00:32:41.292 --> 00:32:44.879
Releasing hatch. Z-0-1 Lancelot,
stand by for activation.

00:32:45.087 --> 00:32:47.006
Initiating pallet extension.

00:32:47.214 --> 00:32:48.174
Have you read the manual?

00:32:48.382 --> 00:32:49.258
More or less.

00:32:49.467 --> 00:32:50.468
Well done.

00:32:50.676 --> 00:32:53.804
| can see how you got
top-class scores in the simulator.

00:32:54.013 --> 00:32:56.640
Listen... that thing we talked about...

00:32:56.849 --> 00:33:01.562
Hmm? Oh. It's possible,
but the possibility's close to zero.

00:33:01.770 --> 00:33:03.939
But not actually zero, right?

00:33:04.148 --> 00:33:06.108
Right, but...

00:33:06.317 --> 00:33:08.611
Still, I don't want you doing anything reckless.

00:33:08.819 --> 00:33:12.156
It's a new system with
no escape mechanism installed.

00:33:12.364 --> 00:33:15.451
Right. I understand, Miss Cécile.

00:33:18.162 --> 00:33:19.371
This is it?

00:33:19.580 --> 00:33:24.335
Yes. The Advanced Special Envoy
Engineering Corps's experimental weapon:

00:33:24.543 --> 00:33:25.794
Lancelot.

00:33:26.003 --> 00:33:30.049
The world's first 7th-generation Knightmare Frame.

00:33:30.257 --> 00:33:33.802
All right then, Suzaku,
shall we proceed with the initial start-up?

00:33:34.011 --> 00:33:36.805
Initial start-up proceeding from phase 20.

00:33:37.014 --> 00:33:38.349
Equipping energy filler.

00:33:38.557 --> 00:33:41.352
Confirm pre-start.
Energy filler now at normal output.

00:33:41.560 --> 00:33:43.395
Thirty seconds to reach critical voltage.

00:33:43.604 --> 00:33:46.398
Core Luminous, shifting phase.
Yggdrasil Drive is in good shape.

00:33:46.607 --> 00:33:51.487
--Devicer, set up.
--Running diagnostics. Power line and drive system statuses green.

00:33:51.695 --> 00:33:53.989
Entry of Devicer to Z-0-1 confirmed.

00:33:54.198 --> 00:33:55.950
Individual I.D. registration completed.

00:33:56.158 --> 00:33:58.327
Establishment of
man-machine interface confirmed.

00:33:58.536 --> 00:34:00.996
Critical voltage reached.
Main system activating.

00:34:01.205 --> 00:34:02.957
--Primary confirmation complete.

00:34:02.957 --> 00:34:04.833
--It's all going according to the data so far.
--Primary confirmation complete.

00:34:05.042 --> 00:34:07.419
Slash harken igniter activated.

00:34:07.628 --> 00:34:10.297
Status of backup tactical bank recognized.

00:34:15.052 --> 00:34:19.181
All systems go. Z-0-1 Lancelot
now prepared to sortie.

00:34:19.390 --> 00:34:22.142
Lancelot, M.E. boost.

00:34:25.062 --> 00:34:26.355
Launch!

00:34:31.068 --> 00:34:33.612
Full throttle, right out of the gate, huh?

00:34:35.155 --> 00:34:38.450
It's better than the manual said! With this...

00:34:38.659 --> 00:34:40.327
Huh? What's that?

00:34:40.536 --> 00:34:42.830
It doesn't look like a Suther--

00:34:44.081 --> 00:34:46.875
This is B-group! Enemy sighted!

00:34:47.084 --> 00:34:49.878
Reinforcements?
Real battle is different, isn't it?

00:34:50.087 --> 00:34:50.963
Status?

00:34:51.171 --> 00:34:54.049
Everyone ejected, but they
took out four units in no time at all!

00:34:54.258 --> 00:34:56.594
--Number of enemies?
--One! Just one!

00:34:56.802 --> 00:35:00.639
| think it's a new model!
I've never seen anything like--

00:35:00.848 --> 00:35:02.516
Hey! What happened?!

00:35:10.649 --> 00:35:13.652
Why, you!

00:35:13.861 --> 00:35:15.571
What? The bullets are bouncing off it?

00:35:15.779 --> 00:35:19.617
Yeah! What should we-- Kimura?!

00:35:19.825 --> 00:35:21.535
Useless terrorists.

00:35:21.744 --> 00:35:24.496
Our resources are more
than enough to take down one unit...

00:35:27.625 --> 00:35:29.209
Dammit!

00:35:32.880 --> 00:35:36.175
Okay! I can do this! With this Lancelot,
| can stop this all at once!

00:35:36.383 --> 00:35:38.302
N-4, N-5, pin it there!

00:35:38.510 --> 00:35:40.054
When the rear unit reaches you, surround it!

00:35:40.262 --> 00:35:41.555
Gotcha!

00:35:47.019 --> 00:35:49.772
We can't stop this thing!

00:35:51.899 --> 00:35:54.526
Hey! What's wrong?!

00:35:54.735 --> 00:35:57.112
What is it? What's happening?

00:35:57.321 --> 00:35:58.530
For heaven's sake.

00:35:58.739 --> 00:36:01.950
Now I'll owe my older brother
a debt I don't need.

00:36:02.159 --> 00:36:04.119
Still, this is for the best.

00:36:09.917 --> 00:36:12.044
P-1, what happened?!

00:36:12.252 --> 00:36:15.756
Is the enemy really just one unit...?!

00:36:22.179 --> 00:36:25.474
If I stop all of the Knightmares,
the battle will end.

00:36:25.683 --> 00:36:28.852
Whatever it takes,
| have to save Lelouch and that girl!

00:36:39.154 --> 00:36:42.032
So this is the unit ruining my plan?!

00:36:42.241 --> 00:36:44.034
You're the commander, aren't you!

00:36:45.369 --> 00:36:48.455
How can a mere pilot
cause me such trouble?!

00:36:52.376 --> 00:36:55.629
No choice! I have to get out of here--

00:37:04.012 --> 00:37:06.515
Hey! I'm returning the favor!

00:37:10.185 --> 00:37:12.312
Is this it for me?

00:37:17.484 --> 00:37:21.488
| see, so the most vital element
in battle is the human one.

00:37:30.914 --> 00:37:33.125
What is that monster?!

00:37:34.752 --> 00:37:38.130
Damn him... He's just causing
more damage for no reason!

00:37:45.846 --> 00:37:49.057
He rescues someone in the midst of battle?

00:37:49.266 --> 00:37:53.562
| don't mind giving you
the tactical victory here. However...

00:37:56.774 --> 00:37:58.525
Huh? He rescued someone?

00:37:58.734 --> 00:38:00.861
So it would seem.

00:38:01.069 --> 00:38:03.655
How strange of him.

00:38:08.202 --> 00:38:10.162
Be careful of his operational time!

00:38:10.370 --> 00:38:10.788
Yes, sir!

00:38:10.996 --> 00:38:15.125
My, that boy is an
excellent piece of equipment!

00:38:15.334 --> 00:38:17.336
Halt! Where's your 1.D.?

00:38:17.544 --> 00:38:19.797
This is Prince Clovis's transport!

00:38:20.005 --> 00:38:21.507
At last, the checkpoint.

00:38:21.715 --> 00:38:23.509
And you're as lightly guarded as I planned.

00:38:23.717 --> 00:38:24.384
Planned?

00:38:24.593 --> 00:38:27.888
Yes. Now, I'd like you to let me pass.

00:38:28.096 --> 00:38:30.349
| see. Understood.

00:38:31.141 --> 00:38:34.144
This only happened because
you guys opposed the Britannians!

00:38:34.353 --> 00:38:36.730
What?! Why, you spineless coward!

00:38:36.939 --> 00:38:38.524
Do you know how many people died?!

00:38:38.732 --> 00:38:42.861
Shut up! Do you know how many
of us were captured or killed?!

00:38:43.070 --> 00:38:43.779
Don't cry!

00:38:43.987 --> 00:38:46.198
Ohgi, what about that guy we heard?

00:38:46.406 --> 00:38:51.078
| don't know. He doesn't answer
when I call. Maybe he's dead.

00:38:54.665 --> 00:38:55.624
There, see?!

00:38:55.833 --> 00:38:57.584
Rather than follow some guy we don't know,

00:38:57.793 --> 00:38:59.586
we should've just used the poison gas!

00:38:59.795 --> 00:39:00.504
But...

00:39:00.712 --> 00:39:02.798
Damn that Nagata!

00:39:04.633 --> 00:39:08.262
So, this is where you Elevens scurried off to.

00:39:08.470 --> 00:39:10.305
Prepare to fire!

00:39:12.307 --> 00:39:13.892
Big brother!

00:39:14.101 --> 00:39:15.769
--Fij--
--Attention, all forces!

00:39:15.978 --> 00:39:18.438
Cease fire at once!

00:39:18.647 --> 00:39:19.273
Cease fire?

00:39:19.481 --> 00:39:21.567
In the name of Clovis la Britannia,

00:39:21.775 --> 00:39:26.071
third prince and royal viceroy
of Area 11, you are so ordered!

00:39:26.280 --> 00:39:28.657
All forces, cease fire at once!

00:39:28.866 --> 00:39:31.743
| shall allow no further fighting!

00:39:33.579 --> 00:39:34.663
Satisfied?

00:39:34.872 --> 00:39:36.623
Yes. Well done.

00:39:36.832 --> 00:39:39.793
What now? A round of songs?

00:39:40.002 --> 00:39:42.170
Or perhaps a nice game of chess?

00:39:42.379 --> 00:39:44.464
That has a familiar ring.

00:39:47.426 --> 00:39:51.346
Don't you remember?
You used to play chess with me.

00:39:51.555 --> 00:39:53.473
Of course, I always won.

00:39:53.682 --> 00:39:54.766
What?

00:39:54.975 --> 00:39:57.477
Remember? At the Aries Villa?

00:39:57.686 --> 00:40:00.981
You... Who are you?!

00:40:01.189 --> 00:40:04.192
It's been a long time, big brother.

00:40:04.401 --> 00:40:09.656
The eldest son of the late Empress Marianne
and 17th in line to the imperial throne...

00:40:09.865 --> 00:40:11.325
...Lelouch vi Britannia, at your service.

00:40:11.533 --> 00:40:14.077
Lelouch?! But I thought...

00:40:14.286 --> 00:40:17.414
That I was dead?

00:40:19.875 --> 00:40:23.795
| have returned, Your Highness.

00:40:24.004 --> 00:40:26.340
To change everything.

00:40:33.347 --> 00:40:35.474
I... I'm so glad, Lelouch!

00:40:35.682 --> 00:40:38.644
| heard you had died
during the capture of Japan.

00:40:38.852 --> 00:40:40.437
Is Nunnally alive, too?

00:40:40.646 --> 00:40:45.067
You're sure talkative when it
comes to imperial successors.

00:40:47.277 --> 00:40:52.282
Mother held the title of Knight of Honor,
but she was originally a commoner.

00:40:52.491 --> 00:40:56.870
No doubt the other
empresses held her in contempt.

00:40:57.079 --> 00:41:00.791
Were you the one who killed her
and made it look like a terrorist attack?

00:41:00.999 --> 00:41:03.251
It wasn't me! I swear, it wasn't!

00:41:03.460 --> 00:41:05.462
Then tell me what you know.

00:41:05.671 --> 00:41:08.507
No one can lie to me now!

00:41:08.715 --> 00:41:11.051
Who killed her?!

00:41:19.184 --> 00:41:25.899
Second prince Schneizel and
second princess Cornelia... they know.

00:41:26.108 --> 00:41:28.235
They're the ringleaders?

00:41:31.113 --> 00:41:33.657
You don't know, huh?

00:41:35.617 --> 00:41:40.330
I-It wasn't me, I swear!
| didn't kill her! Or have her killed!

00:41:40.539 --> 00:41:42.541
| understand.

00:41:42.749 --> 00:41:44.793
However...

00:41:45.002 --> 00:41:48.755
No, don't! We may have different mothers,
but I'm still your brother!

00:41:51.049 --> 00:41:52.676
Wake up, Lelouch!

00:41:52.884 --> 00:41:55.345
You were asleep just now!
Your hand stopped moving!

00:41:55.554 --> 00:41:57.556
You don't have to beat me up for it!

00:41:57.764 --> 00:41:59.891
That's what you get for ditching me before!

00:42:00.100 --> 00:42:02.477
Yeah, what were you up to yesterday?

00:42:02.686 --> 00:42:03.520
Uh, nothing...

00:42:03.729 --> 00:42:07.107
All right, all right! No changing the subject!

00:42:07.315 --> 00:42:10.235
If we don't review the club budgets now,

00:42:10.444 --> 00:42:11.862
no clubs will get any money, will they?

00:42:12.070 --> 00:42:13.405
And if that happens...

00:42:13.613 --> 00:42:15.365
The horseback riding club will be pissed off!

00:42:15.574 --> 00:42:18.910
They'll come busting in here again!

00:42:19.119 --> 00:42:22.080
Rivalz, can't you take being on
the student council more seriously?

00:42:22.289 --> 00:42:26.209
You should have reminded us
about the deadline a day earlier.

00:42:26.418 --> 00:42:29.296
I'd have preferred a day later.
Then we could give up.

00:42:29.504 --> 00:42:30.881
Good idea. Why not do that now?

00:42:31.089 --> 00:42:33.425
Guts!

00:42:33.633 --> 00:42:36.053
Casting your "Guts!" spell again?

00:42:36.261 --> 00:42:39.639
Yup! Don't you want to work harder now?

00:42:39.848 --> 00:42:42.267
A fake spell like that will never work.

00:42:42.476 --> 00:42:44.644
I'll pretend it's working on me, Prez!

00:42:44.853 --> 00:42:46.813
Good! A sound body leads
to a well-behaved mind, I see.

00:42:47.022 --> 00:42:48.899
Gotta call me well-trained!

00:42:49.107 --> 00:42:51.610
That's not what I meant.

00:42:51.818 --> 00:42:53.820
You're impressive.

00:42:54.029 --> 00:42:57.074
| checked you out in the girls' bathroom.

00:42:57.282 --> 00:42:59.576
Your top and bottom are very nicely balanced.

00:42:59.785 --> 00:43:00.786
Oh ho!

00:43:00.994 --> 00:43:03.705
Wh-What are you talking about, you pervert?!

00:43:07.584 --> 00:43:09.878
That ex-bureaucrat's
response is tepid at best.

00:43:10.087 --> 00:43:11.588
You mean General Bartley?

00:43:11.797 --> 00:43:15.092
The perpetrator broke
into high-security areas twice.

00:43:15.300 --> 00:43:17.385
Such a perfunctory inspection won't find him!

00:43:17.594 --> 00:43:22.682
Margrave Jeremiah, now that
Prince Clovis is dead, we Purebloods can...

00:43:22.891 --> 00:43:24.392
I'll give the directions.

00:43:24.601 --> 00:43:27.229
Wait until I've gotten everyone on our side.

00:43:27.437 --> 00:43:28.897
Kallen! It's been ages!

00:43:29.106 --> 00:43:30.315
Are you okay?

00:43:30.524 --> 00:43:32.484
Sophie's been worried about you.

00:43:32.692 --> 00:43:34.027
You're okay now?

00:43:34.236 --> 00:43:37.405
Yes, although I can't strain myself.

00:43:41.827 --> 00:43:44.663
And if I take too much time off,
I'll never be able to keep up with everyone.

00:43:44.871 --> 00:43:47.541
Whatcha looking at, my dear Lelouch?

00:43:47.749 --> 00:43:49.501
Might you have a crush on her?

00:43:49.709 --> 00:43:51.753
Just thinking this is a rare event.

00:43:51.962 --> 00:43:54.840
She hasn't been here since the term started.

00:43:55.048 --> 00:43:57.884
Kallen Stadtfeld.

00:43:58.093 --> 00:44:00.387
| hear she isn't well.

00:44:00.595 --> 00:44:02.973
She was barely in school last year, too.

00:44:03.181 --> 00:44:05.267
Still, her grades are at the top of the class.

00:44:05.475 --> 00:44:10.313
Since she's a daughter of the Stadtfeld family,
she's got wealth and a gentle disposition.

00:44:10.522 --> 00:44:12.774
Man, you have good taste!

00:44:12.983 --> 00:44:16.611
Though she's a touch
too sheltered, if you ask me.

00:44:18.989 --> 00:44:20.240
A bee! There's a bee!

00:44:20.448 --> 00:44:23.034
Kallen, run!

00:44:26.997 --> 00:44:29.749
Hurry and run!

00:44:32.043 --> 00:44:35.297
What's a bee doing in here?

00:44:35.505 --> 00:44:38.091
| wonder if there's a hive nearby.

00:44:40.385 --> 00:44:42.220
Oh, this pisses me off!

00:44:42.429 --> 00:44:45.891
| wish I didn't have
to act like a freaking invalid!

00:44:48.226 --> 00:44:50.645
Crap! He saw me!

00:44:51.104 --> 00:44:54.149
C-Can I help you?

00:44:54.357 --> 00:44:56.276
Answer my questions.

00:45:02.115 --> 00:45:03.116
Yes.

00:45:03.325 --> 00:45:06.077
You piloted that Glasgow
in Shinjuku yesterday, didn't you?

00:45:06.286 --> 00:45:07.245
Yes.

00:45:07.454 --> 00:45:08.872
Why are you a terrorist?

00:45:09.080 --> 00:45:14.085
Because I'm Japanese.
Although I am technically half-Britannian.

00:45:14.294 --> 00:45:15.754
A half-breed?!

00:45:15.962 --> 00:45:18.757
But why go that far?

00:45:24.304 --> 00:45:26.431
Um... Did you want something?

00:45:26.640 --> 00:45:29.559
No. I'm through here.

00:45:29.768 --> 00:45:33.188
Right. Just to be sure...

00:45:33.396 --> 00:45:36.024
Don't say anything about
what happened in Shinjuku.

00:45:36.233 --> 00:45:39.069
What do you mean in Shinjuku?

00:45:39.277 --> 00:45:40.695
What makes you mention that?

00:45:40.904 --> 00:45:42.113
Return to the classroom.

00:45:42.322 --> 00:45:44.699
Only if you answer that question!

00:45:44.908 --> 00:45:48.161
It's not working?! What's going on here?

00:45:49.704 --> 00:45:52.958
What shall we do?
He may be late again tonight.

00:45:53.166 --> 00:45:57.003
I'll wait. He said we'd eat dinner together.

00:45:58.088 --> 00:46:00.924
Look, it's all done.

00:46:08.056 --> 00:46:08.974
A bird?

00:46:09.182 --> 00:46:10.475
Right. It's a crane.

00:46:10.684 --> 00:46:14.521
Amazing. Japanese people are so skillful!

00:46:16.481 --> 00:46:18.650
Miss Nunnally?

00:46:20.277 --> 00:46:22.028
Sorry I'm so late.

00:46:22.237 --> 00:46:24.114
Welcome home, big brother!

00:46:24.322 --> 00:46:26.116
Welcome home, sir.

00:46:26.324 --> 00:46:29.494
I'm home, Nunnally. Miss Sayoko.

00:46:29.703 --> 00:46:34.207
As you all know, the project
was a complete failure.

00:46:34.416 --> 00:46:36.751
Consequently, I am disbanding
this research center.

00:46:36.960 --> 00:46:38.044
What?! But--

00:46:38.253 --> 00:46:40.046
I've set up a place in Narita for you.

00:46:40.255 --> 00:46:41.548
Move everything out there.

00:46:41.756 --> 00:46:43.091
While none of us remember doing so,

00:46:43.300 --> 00:46:47.762
the fact is that I and the other staff
officers left Prince Clovis on his own.

00:46:47.971 --> 00:46:51.433
I'll very likely be recalled to the
homeland to take responsibility for that.

00:46:51.641 --> 00:46:54.060
When I do, if His Majesty
learns that this experiment

00:46:54.269 --> 00:46:57.272
was carried out without his knowledge...

00:46:57.480 --> 00:47:00.275
Understood, sir! We'll make
preparations as fast as we can!

00:47:00.483 --> 00:47:04.988
Miss Sayoko was just
teaching me about origami.

00:47:05.196 --> 00:47:07.407
When you fold a piece
of paper over and over,

00:47:07.615 --> 00:47:13.079
you can make birds and boats
and all sorts of things!

00:47:13.288 --> 00:47:16.207
You really don't have to talk so fast.

00:47:16.416 --> 00:47:18.043
I'm not going anywhere.

00:47:18.251 --> 00:47:20.253
Thank you, big brother.

00:47:20.462 --> 00:47:22.255
You're very welcome.

00:47:22.464 --> 00:47:23.506
I'm so glad.

00:47:23.715 --> 00:47:27.427
You were sort of scary last night.

00:47:27.635 --> 00:47:31.348
Was 1? Sorry. I had something to think about.

00:47:31.556 --> 00:47:33.099
So...

00:47:33.308 --> 00:47:37.145
They say if you fold a thousand cranes,
your wish comes true.

00:47:37.354 --> 00:47:40.023
So, if you have anything to wish for...

00:47:40.231 --> 00:47:41.983
Oh, no. Not me.

00:47:42.192 --> 00:47:44.903
And you, Nunnally?
Do you wish for anything?

00:47:46.321 --> 00:47:48.990
| wish the world was a gentle place.

00:47:49.199 --> 00:47:52.911
When you can see again, I'm sure it will be.

00:47:53.119 --> 00:47:54.454
Really?!

00:47:54.662 --> 00:47:56.664
| promise.

00:47:56.873 --> 00:47:57.874
That's right.

00:47:58.083 --> 00:48:00.919
There are few futures which are open to us.

00:48:01.127 --> 00:48:03.046
While they may be sheltering us here,

00:48:03.254 --> 00:48:06.466
will the Ashford family
always be there to back us up?

00:48:06.674 --> 00:48:11.054
Our fate is to be either political tools
or the victims of conspiracy.

00:48:11.262 --> 00:48:17.435
| have to make a world where Nunnally,
at least, can live happily.

00:48:17.644 --> 00:48:21.523
She taught me about this before.
It's how the Japanese make a promise.

00:48:21.731 --> 00:48:28.196
Cross my heart, hope to die,
eat a thousand needles if I lie.

00:48:30.323 --> 00:48:33.660
That's scary stuff! Liars have
to eat a thousand needles?

00:48:33.868 --> 00:48:37.705
Uh-huh! So you'd better not be lying.

00:48:37.914 --> 00:48:40.166
So, how's life at your dear old school?

00:48:40.375 --> 00:48:41.418
Stifling.

00:48:41.626 --> 00:48:44.003
| had history class yesterday!

00:48:44.212 --> 00:48:45.964
Look, maybe I should head back to you.

00:48:46.172 --> 00:48:48.299
The army's on high alert right now.

00:48:48.508 --> 00:48:50.802
Stay there and let things cool down.

00:48:51.010 --> 00:48:52.804
But what about the voice on the radio?

00:48:53.012 --> 00:48:56.224
We can't go looking for a voice. Besides...

00:48:56.433 --> 00:49:00.895
Naoto would be happier to have you in school.

00:49:01.104 --> 00:49:03.189
Firstly, the education of the aristocracy.

00:49:03.398 --> 00:49:07.360
Concentrating on the ruling class
with intensive education and training

00:49:07.569 --> 00:49:08.736
produces a superior breed of rulers.

00:49:08.945 --> 00:49:10.947
--It's similar, maybe...
--Secondly, speed.

00:49:11.156 --> 00:49:14.659
--No, I don't remember the voice well enough to be sure.
--Since only a small number of the very best are chosen to rule,

00:49:14.868 --> 00:49:17.203
decisions can be made very quickly.

00:49:17.412 --> 00:49:19.372
All right, that will do.

00:49:19.581 --> 00:49:23.835
With the ascension of Henry XI,
son of the great Elizabeth |,

00:49:24.043 --> 00:49:25.336
the House of Tudor
reached its greatest height.

00:49:25.545 --> 00:49:29.090
All I gave her was the word
"Shinjuku."” However...

00:49:29.299 --> 00:49:31.593
If he knows who I really am...

00:49:31.801 --> 00:49:32.886
As soon as possible...

00:49:33.094 --> 00:49:34.971
...| need to take care of him.

00:49:37.807 --> 00:49:38.641
And the research center?

00:49:38.850 --> 00:49:40.435
It was transferred to Narita last night.

00:49:40.643 --> 00:49:42.353
| see.

00:49:42.562 --> 00:49:45.023
Forgive me, Your Highness.

00:49:51.112 --> 00:49:52.071
General Bartley!

00:49:52.280 --> 00:49:52.780
What is it?

00:49:52.989 --> 00:49:56.284
Sir, the Purebloods just sent
word that they'll be taking over.

00:49:56.493 --> 00:49:59.329
What? Do they mean to pull a coup d'état?

00:50:01.748 --> 00:50:04.459
Do you understand our determination now?

00:50:04.667 --> 00:50:06.461
B-But, I told you!

00:50:06.669 --> 00:50:08.087
You " !
don't remember"?

00:50:08.296 --> 00:50:11.174
You still cling to that
pathetic excuse of yours?!

00:50:11.382 --> 00:50:13.801
Ask the others! If you want the testimony...

00:50:14.010 --> 00:50:16.304
Ducking the blame! You're a disgrace!

00:50:16.513 --> 00:50:19.974
| won't allow you to remain
at His Highness's side any longer!

00:50:20.183 --> 00:50:22.602
| never knew there was
anyplace like this in the school.

00:50:22.810 --> 00:50:25.146
It's the club house for use
by the student council.

00:50:25.355 --> 00:50:28.399
It was built large enough
to host a formal dance.

00:50:28.608 --> 00:50:30.693
So, what did you want to talk about?

00:50:30.902 --> 00:50:32.403
There it is!

00:50:32.612 --> 00:50:34.989
Found it! Look, it's this, right?

00:50:35.198 --> 00:50:37.617
Ah! That's it! The experimental data.

00:50:37.825 --> 00:50:40.662
Oh, man... My back hurts now.

00:50:40.870 --> 00:50:42.205
Did you find it?

00:50:42.413 --> 00:50:44.374
I'm through on my end, so why don't we start?

00:50:44.582 --> 00:50:45.583
Whoa! Amazing!

00:50:45.792 --> 00:50:47.835
Way to go, Milly!

00:50:48.044 --> 00:50:50.547
Please, you can compliment me more!

00:50:50.755 --> 00:50:52.590
Um... What is all this?

00:50:52.799 --> 00:50:55.426
Didn't you bring her here because you knew?

00:50:55.635 --> 00:50:57.345
We're letting Kallen into the student council.

00:50:57.554 --> 00:50:58.096
What?

00:50:58.304 --> 00:51:00.306
My grandfather asked us to.

00:51:00.515 --> 00:51:01.015
The school principal did?

00:51:01.224 --> 00:51:03.476
Yeah. He says it would be hard
for her to be in a regular club

00:51:03.685 --> 00:51:06.020
because of her health problems.

00:51:06.229 --> 00:51:09.232
Oh! I'm Milly, the council president.
How do you do?

00:51:09.440 --> 00:51:12.026
Er, it's a pleasure to meet you.

00:51:12.235 --> 00:51:13.987
I'm Rivalz, the secretary.

00:51:14.195 --> 00:51:16.155
If there's anything you
don't understand, just ask me.

00:51:16.364 --> 00:51:19.701
I'm Shirley, and I'm also
in the swim club. How do you do?

00:51:19.909 --> 00:51:22.120
And, I'm Nina.

00:51:22.328 --> 00:51:24.205
Um, uh, a pleasure.

00:51:24.414 --> 00:51:28.793
Excuse me, Shirley, but could
you put these on the table for me?

00:51:29.002 --> 00:51:30.378
Oh, thanks, Nunna!

00:51:30.587 --> 00:51:32.463
Nunnally? You, too?

00:51:33.464 --> 00:51:34.674
This is Lelouch's little sister.

00:51:34.882 --> 00:51:38.386
I'm not in the student council,
though, since I'm in middle school.

00:51:38.595 --> 00:51:40.680
That's okay. You're an
associate member, right?

00:51:40.888 --> 00:51:41.889
Right.

00:51:42.098 --> 00:51:45.393
It's a pleasure to meet you, Kallen.

00:51:45.602 --> 00:51:47.979
It's a pleasure for me, too.

00:51:49.022 --> 00:51:53.234
Breaking news:
Viceroy Clovis has passed away.

00:51:53.443 --> 00:51:55.903
| repeat, Viceroy Clovis has passed away.

00:51:56.112 --> 00:51:59.907
We go now to Acting Consul
Jeremiah Gottwald's press conference

00:52:00.116 --> 00:52:02.201
in the State building.

00:52:02.410 --> 00:52:04.704
Prince Clovis met his death

00:52:04.912 --> 00:52:08.333
during a battle to protect peace
and justice from terrorists.

00:52:08.541 --> 00:52:13.630
We all must push down
our sorrow and carry on his will!

00:52:13.838 --> 00:52:16.716
We've just received new information.

00:52:16.924 --> 00:52:19.302
The murderer has been captured.

00:52:19.510 --> 00:52:23.723
According to the report, the man
arrested is an honorary Britannian:

00:52:23.931 --> 00:52:25.683
Private Suzaku Kururugi.

00:52:25.892 --> 00:52:28.061
The suspect is a former Eleven--

00:52:28.269 --> 00:52:33.650
You know what this weapon is,
don't you, Suzaku Kururugi?

00:52:33.858 --> 00:52:36.277
It was the one used
to assassinate Prince Clovis.

00:52:36.486 --> 00:52:38.404
The barrel striations confirm this.

00:52:38.613 --> 00:52:41.324
| also took the liberty of investigating you.

00:52:41.532 --> 00:52:45.411
You're the son of Japan's
last prime minister, aren't you?

00:52:45.620 --> 00:52:47.121
You had plenty of motive.

00:52:47.330 --> 00:52:51.167
This is some sort of mistake!
I've never seen that gun in my--

00:52:51.376 --> 00:52:54.170
Your fingerprints showed up on it.

00:52:54.379 --> 00:52:57.215
You're also suspected of
murdering members of the royal guard.

00:52:57.423 --> 00:52:58.383
Admit it now,

00:52:58.591 --> 00:53:02.470
and you'll be judged as an honorary
Britannian instead of as an Eleven.

00:53:02.679 --> 00:53:06.391
| didn't do it!

00:53:06.599 --> 00:53:10.103
That was Suzaku they mentioned
on the news, wasn't it?

00:53:10.311 --> 00:53:13.064
Yeah. It looks like Suzaku's still alive.

00:53:13.272 --> 00:53:19.529
Yeah. We've been apart since
the war ended, so even we might...

00:53:19.737 --> 00:53:20.697
Big brother?

00:53:20.905 --> 00:53:21.656
What?

00:53:21.864 --> 00:53:23.658
That news wasn't true, was it?

00:53:23.866 --> 00:53:25.243
It wasn't.

00:53:25.451 --> 00:53:29.372
Suzaku would never do anything like that.
It's some kind of mistake.

00:53:29.580 --> 00:53:31.582
Yes... It must be.

00:53:31.791 --> 00:53:34.377
Right. So...

00:53:34.585 --> 00:53:36.754
Good night, Nunnally.

00:53:36.963 --> 00:53:40.508
Aw, we've lost our most essential part!

00:53:40.717 --> 00:53:42.093
Can't we make do without him?

00:53:42.301 --> 00:53:43.636
| wish.

00:53:43.845 --> 00:53:46.973
Most pilots are with rigid
organizations we can't mobilize.

00:53:47.181 --> 00:53:50.476
And even if we could,
they wouldn't get readings like he did.

00:53:50.685 --> 00:53:52.937
Then you should speak up
so they'll release Suzaku!

00:53:53.146 --> 00:53:55.690
He's only an honorary Britannian.

00:53:55.898 --> 00:53:57.358
Since General Bartley's disgrace,

00:53:57.567 --> 00:54:00.403
the Purebloods have been
in control of the military.

00:54:00.611 --> 00:54:03.740
Huh? You heard from the man in Shinjuku?

00:54:04.782 --> 00:54:08.369
Nah, I don't think this "Lelouch” is our guy.

00:54:08.578 --> 00:54:12.790
Considering his sister, he can't
afford any anti-Britannia resistance.

00:54:12.999 --> 00:54:17.086
Huh. I guess it was someone else
who contacted us, then.

00:54:17.295 --> 00:54:18.004
What did he want?

00:54:18.212 --> 00:54:21.883
He asked if we were interested
in rescuing Suzaku Kururugi.

00:54:22.091 --> 00:54:28.890
It's true that our team would
get bigger if we rescued him, but...

00:54:29.098 --> 00:54:32.185
His Highness's memorial program
was handled very well.

00:54:32.393 --> 00:54:34.520
A bit too weepy for my tastes, but...

00:54:34.729 --> 00:54:38.191
Your Excellency,
the masses enjoy a tearjerker.

00:54:38.399 --> 00:54:42.695
Spoken like a true TV man.
Still, I acknowledge your skills.

00:54:42.904 --> 00:54:45.198
You did well in the short time you had.

00:54:45.406 --> 00:54:48.701
One would almost think you
were expecting His Highness to die.

00:54:48.910 --> 00:54:53.706
I'm afraid it's quite common to have memorial
programs prepared for important people.

00:54:53.915 --> 00:54:55.291
For me as well?

00:54:55.500 --> 00:54:59.086
After this, we may make
one for you, Your Excellency.

00:54:59.295 --> 00:55:02.131
Meaning I wasn't important
enough to rate one until now.

00:55:02.340 --> 00:55:03.633
How honest of you!

00:55:03.841 --> 00:55:05.468
I'm afraid so.

00:55:05.676 --> 00:55:08.554
Feel like joining the army?
We have a need for information officers.

00:55:08.763 --> 00:55:12.266
| have to admit that I'm not up to that job.

00:55:12.475 --> 00:55:17.271
You prefer a civilian network? No matter.
| have another favor to ask of you.

00:55:17.480 --> 00:55:21.400
Tomorrow night, Suzaku Kururugi
will be transported to a military court.

00:55:21.609 --> 00:55:25.363
I'll get a crowd of patriotic
Britannians to line the roadside.

00:55:25.571 --> 00:55:27.490
It's helpful that you catch on so quickly.

00:55:27.698 --> 00:55:29.867
Be sure his face can be
seen clearly in the convoy.

00:55:30.076 --> 00:55:32.245
Lord Jeremiah, there are
some among the Elevens

00:55:32.453 --> 00:55:35.248
who have made
Private Kururugi out to be a hero.

00:55:35.456 --> 00:55:37.583
Some groups may even be
thinking of freeing him.

00:55:37.792 --> 00:55:40.169
I'll be providing security
personally in my Sutherland.

00:55:40.378 --> 00:55:44.549
If they have the temerity to try,
I'll execute them on the spot!

00:55:46.676 --> 00:55:50.638
Next station: Okubo. Okubo.

00:55:50.847 --> 00:55:54.433
Change there for the Chuo Soubu line.

00:55:54.642 --> 00:55:56.018
Hello?

00:55:58.479 --> 00:56:03.401
Face forward and look to your right.
What do you see?

00:56:03.609 --> 00:56:05.653
The Britannians' city.

00:56:05.862 --> 00:56:09.574
A stolen city, built on our sacrifices.

00:56:09.782 --> 00:56:11.868
And to your left?

00:56:12.076 --> 00:56:13.870
| see our city.

00:56:14.078 --> 00:56:17.290
A dried-up husk after
Britannia squeezed us dry.

00:56:17.498 --> 00:56:19.375
Good answer.

00:56:19.584 --> 00:56:22.461
All right, come to the forward car.

00:56:31.721 --> 00:56:35.308
Is it you?

00:56:35.516 --> 00:56:37.768
This isn't a trap, is it?

00:56:41.480 --> 00:56:44.942
Tell us! Was it you in Shinjuku?
Was the cease-fire order your doing, too?

00:56:45.151 --> 00:56:47.904
Hey! Say something!

00:56:50.406 --> 00:56:53.242
Well? How was your tour of the settlement?

00:56:53.451 --> 00:56:54.243
Tour?

00:56:54.452 --> 00:56:57.246
Hey, it couldn't have been this joker!

00:56:57.455 --> 00:56:59.832
| wanted you to have a
proper understanding of them.

00:57:00.041 --> 00:57:02.043
Of the settlement and the ghetto!

00:57:02.251 --> 00:57:05.463
Yes, there's a difference
between us and the Britannians!

00:57:05.671 --> 00:57:06.964
A desperate difference!

00:57:07.173 --> 00:57:08.382
That's why we fight as the resistance!

00:57:08.591 --> 00:57:10.384
You're wrong.

00:57:10.593 --> 00:57:12.678
Terrorism will not defeat Britannia!

00:57:12.887 --> 00:57:13.679
"Defeat"?

00:57:13.888 --> 00:57:16.641
Terrorism is merely a childish nuisance.

00:57:16.849 --> 00:57:17.934
What was that?!

00:57:18.142 --> 00:57:19.518
Are you saying we're just kids?!

00:57:19.727 --> 00:57:24.523
Don't mistake your enemy. It isn't the
Britannian people, but Britannia itself!

00:57:24.732 --> 00:57:26.150
What you need to fight is a war!

00:57:26.359 --> 00:57:27.985
Do not involve civilians!

00:57:28.194 --> 00:57:31.948
Make up your minds!
Take the path of righteousness!

00:57:32.156 --> 00:57:35.242
Don't be absurd!
It's easy to say whatever you want!

00:57:35.451 --> 00:57:38.412
As if we could trust someone
who won't even show us his face!

00:57:38.621 --> 00:57:39.080
She's right!

00:57:39.288 --> 00:57:40.164
Take off the mask!

00:57:40.373 --> 00:57:43.000
Yeah. Can we ask you
to show us your face?

00:57:43.209 --> 00:57:46.212
Very well. I'll show you.

00:57:46.420 --> 00:57:50.049
However, what I'll show you won't be
my face, but rather my power!

00:57:50.257 --> 00:57:52.635
If I show you that the impossible is possible,

00:57:52.843 --> 00:57:55.346
you'll trust me a little, won't you?

00:57:56.681 --> 00:58:00.101
Any moment. Any moment now!

00:58:00.309 --> 00:58:03.604
Just look at the crowds lining the route.

00:58:03.813 --> 00:58:07.233
All of them, waiting! Waiting for the man
accused of killing Prince Clovis!

00:58:07.441 --> 00:58:10.486
Waiting for honorary
Britannian Suzaku Kururugi to pass by!

00:58:10.695 --> 00:58:14.407
Waiting with bated breath
for the former Eleven!

00:58:14.615 --> 00:58:18.953
Camera 5's slow. Charles?
Have you got your crowd set up?

00:58:19.161 --> 00:58:21.706
Huh? The studio? Let 'em wait.

00:58:21.914 --> 00:58:24.792
There's no delay.
Everything's going as planned--

00:58:25.001 --> 00:58:26.502
Ah, that's him.

00:58:26.711 --> 00:58:29.171
They're coming into view!
It's Kururugi, the suspect!

00:58:29.380 --> 00:58:31.757
Suzaku Kururugi will be here soon!

00:58:31.966 --> 00:58:34.343
There, you see?

00:58:34.552 --> 00:58:37.304
This sham... How far I've fallen.

00:58:37.513 --> 00:58:38.723
--Murderer!
--Scum!

00:58:38.931 --> 00:58:42.893
--Damned Eleven!
--We want our prince back!

00:58:43.853 --> 00:58:46.981
We're hearing voices shouting
in resentment, in anger!

00:58:47.189 --> 00:58:50.192
Voices giving proof of the love
the prince's people had for him.

00:58:50.401 --> 00:58:52.987
Righteous voices which judge the terrorist!

00:58:53.195 --> 00:58:54.697
Suzaku!

00:58:56.490 --> 00:58:59.994
Margrave Jeremiah himself,
whose efforts helped to settle this case,

00:59:00.202 --> 00:59:03.122
has assumed command as acting consul.

00:59:07.835 --> 00:59:10.838
There's no way just the
three of them can do this!

00:59:19.055 --> 00:59:23.809
Now that I've begun walking
this path, I don't need a way back.

00:59:24.018 --> 00:59:25.394
Acting Consul Jeremiah!

00:59:25.603 --> 00:59:26.145
What is it?

00:59:26.353 --> 00:59:28.731
Vehicle approaching the
main highway from Third Street.

00:59:28.939 --> 00:59:30.733
We let it pass as instructed, but...

00:59:30.941 --> 00:59:32.902
Do you think it's a terrorist vehicle?

00:59:33.110 --> 00:59:35.571
Well, sir... It's Prince Clovis's car.

00:59:35.780 --> 00:59:37.281
The prince's?!

00:59:37.490 --> 00:59:41.702
This guy's a joker. Never mind.
Let him through to us!

00:59:41.911 --> 00:59:44.163
All forces, halt!

00:59:44.371 --> 00:59:45.873
They stopped! They really did!

00:59:46.082 --> 00:59:47.708
Heh! It's a coincidence!

00:59:47.917 --> 00:59:52.046
But he did say Jeremiah likes
being the center of attention...

00:59:52.254 --> 00:59:53.047
Coincidence!

00:59:53.255 --> 00:59:55.966
No stop was scheduled here.

00:59:56.175 --> 00:59:58.094
Could there have been some sort of accident?

00:59:58.302 --> 01:00:01.639
This is site 5!
There's a vehicle approaching them!

01:00:02.681 --> 01:00:05.559
It... It's Prince Clovis's personal transport!

01:00:05.768 --> 01:00:08.062
--Impossible! He's coming straight at them!
--Can you see it? It's headed towards you!

01:00:08.270 --> 01:00:10.564
What's he planning?

01:00:12.149 --> 01:00:15.027
Will they really buy this fake?

01:00:18.614 --> 01:00:22.785
Show yourself, you who dare
to sully His Highness's transport!

01:00:28.332 --> 01:00:31.127
| am... Zero!

01:00:31.335 --> 01:00:32.044
Zero?

01:00:32.253 --> 01:00:34.672
Wh-Who could this be?!

01:00:34.880 --> 01:00:38.425
A man calling himself Zero is
standing in the path of the convoy!

01:00:38.634 --> 01:00:39.969
What is all this?!

01:00:40.177 --> 01:00:40.970
--Does he have some connection to the suspect?

01:00:40.970 --> 01:00:43.180
--What's he doing?!
--Does he have some connection to the suspect?

01:00:43.389 --> 01:00:46.308
We don't know anything at this point.

01:00:46.517 --> 01:00:49.019
Who is this man calling himself Zero?

01:00:49.228 --> 01:00:52.273
--Zero? As in nothing?
--No one has used the code name "Zero" before.

01:00:52.273 --> 01:00:54.441
--Is it an Eleven?
--No one has used the code name "Zero" before.

01:00:54.650 --> 01:00:57.027
Suzaku... Now to return the favor.

01:00:57.236 --> 01:01:01.699
Had enough, Zero?
Your little show is at an end!

01:01:07.913 --> 01:01:11.709
Now, first you can remove that mask.

01:01:17.298 --> 01:01:18.007
What?!

01:01:18.215 --> 01:01:20.009
Your Excellency, that's...!

01:01:20.217 --> 01:01:22.011
Yes, Jeremiah.

01:01:22.219 --> 01:01:26.182
As you never saw what was inside,
you assume this is a poison gas capsule.

01:01:26.390 --> 01:01:28.392
No! That's--

01:01:28.601 --> 01:01:30.811
Can all of you watching TV now see this?

01:01:31.020 --> 01:01:33.981
It's some sort of device,
although its purpose is unclear.

01:01:34.190 --> 01:01:39.111
Let's keep watching and
see if this assumed terrorist explains.

01:01:39.320 --> 01:01:40.738
Th-That bastard...

01:01:40.946 --> 01:01:43.908
He's taken every Britannian here hostage!

01:01:44.116 --> 01:01:47.995
And without them even
knowing they're hostages!

01:01:48.204 --> 01:01:49.496
Want to shoot me?

01:01:49.705 --> 01:01:54.835
-- I think you know what'll happen if you try.
--Unit 6, bring up the sound! And get the camera in closer! Right in his face!

01:01:55.044 --> 01:01:57.046
But sir, this is dangerous!

01:01:57.254 --> 01:01:59.256
Amateur!

01:02:01.300 --> 01:02:03.093
Very well. Your demands?

01:02:03.302 --> 01:02:05.679
An exchange. This for Suzaku Kururugi.

01:02:05.888 --> 01:02:08.682
Absurd! This man is charged with high treason

01:02:08.891 --> 01:02:11.977
for the murder of Prince Clovis!
| can't hand him over!

01:02:12.186 --> 01:02:14.980
No, you're mistaken, Jeremiah.

01:02:15.189 --> 01:02:18.984
He isn't the murderer.

01:02:19.193 --> 01:02:22.947
The man who killed Clovis... was me!

01:02:23.155 --> 01:02:24.156
--No way!
--Him?

01:02:24.365 --> 01:02:25.908
Seriously?!

01:02:26.951 --> 01:02:28.786
--I don't believe it!
--The real killer!

01:02:28.994 --> 01:02:31.080
He claims to be the real culprit.

01:02:31.288 --> 01:02:34.792
So, where does this leave the
currently imprisoned Private Kururugi?!

01:02:35.000 --> 01:02:37.086
He's gone too far! We can't escape!

01:02:37.294 --> 01:02:38.671
It's hopeless now!

01:02:38.879 --> 01:02:42.841
For a single Eleven, you'll save
the lives of many precious Britannians.

01:02:43.050 --> 01:02:45.552
| don't think it's such a bad deal for you.

01:02:45.761 --> 01:02:48.764
He's playing this whole thing like it's a show!

01:02:48.973 --> 01:02:50.599
He's insane!

01:02:50.808 --> 01:02:53.185
Disguising this truck as
His Highness's, and mocking us!

01:02:53.394 --> 01:02:54.979
We'll make him pay!

01:02:55.187 --> 01:02:59.024
Are you sure about this?
I'll make it all public, Orange.

01:02:59.233 --> 01:03:00.693
What's "Orange"?

01:03:00.901 --> 01:03:02.319
| don't know.

01:03:05.864 --> 01:03:10.244
If I die, it'll all go public.
If you don't want that to happen...

01:03:10.452 --> 01:03:12.997
What are you talking about?
What are you saying?!

01:03:13.205 --> 01:03:17.334
Let us go with all your might.
That man you hold as well!

01:03:25.801 --> 01:03:26.802
Understood.

01:03:27.011 --> 01:03:29.138
Give them the prisoner!

01:03:29.346 --> 01:03:31.098
Lord Jeremiah, what did you just say?!

01:03:31.307 --> 01:03:33.600
Give them the prisoner!

01:03:33.809 --> 01:03:34.685
Should we?

01:03:34.893 --> 01:03:35.728
But...

01:03:35.936 --> 01:03:38.355
Let them have him! Nobody interfere!

01:03:38.564 --> 01:03:40.482
What are you thinking,
making a deal like this?!

01:03:40.691 --> 01:03:43.027
Lord Kewell! This is an order!

01:03:43.235 --> 01:03:45.863
| can't tell from here what happened,

01:03:46.071 --> 01:03:48.907
but it looks like Suzaku Kururugi's
release has been arranged!

01:03:55.789 --> 01:03:57.416
Who the hell...?

01:03:57.624 --> 01:04:00.878
| didn't expect they'd allow you to speak.

01:04:05.716 --> 01:04:07.968
If they get away, we'll be disgraced!

01:04:08.177 --> 01:04:09.178
Zero, it's time.

01:04:09.386 --> 01:04:11.805
Then we'll talk later.

01:04:14.308 --> 01:04:16.560
You cowardly Elevens!

01:04:16.769 --> 01:04:17.936
Lord Jeremiah, why?!

01:04:18.145 --> 01:04:20.647
| told you not to interfere!

01:04:22.274 --> 01:04:24.985
They jumped?!
They must have accomplices!

01:04:30.699 --> 01:04:32.826
It worked! Now we can--

01:04:34.286 --> 01:04:36.622
Fools! You thought you'd escape
from amidst our guards?!

01:04:36.830 --> 01:04:38.248
Lord Kewell!

01:04:38.457 --> 01:04:40.376
Will you follow my orders or not?!

01:04:40.584 --> 01:04:42.878
Any further actions will result in punishment.

01:04:43.087 --> 01:04:45.089
Relay this order to all units! Is that clear?!

01:04:45.297 --> 01:04:48.300
Let them go with all your might!

01:04:53.138 --> 01:04:55.516
| really didn't think he'd save him.

01:04:55.724 --> 01:04:57.267
Who is that guy?

01:04:57.476 --> 01:05:00.854
This is bull! How many times
can a bluff like that work?!

01:05:01.063 --> 01:05:03.023
But there's something you have to admit.

01:05:03.232 --> 01:05:03.690
Huh?

01:05:03.899 --> 01:05:06.860
Who else but him could have pulled that off?

01:05:07.069 --> 01:05:09.321
Even the Japan Liberation Front
couldn't do this.

01:05:09.530 --> 01:05:12.574
Or at least, I can't do it.

01:05:12.783 --> 01:05:16.453
We all thought that war with
the Britannians was impossible.

01:05:16.662 --> 01:05:19.081
But maybe, with him, it's possible.

01:05:21.250 --> 01:05:24.044
Looks like they treated you very roughly.

01:05:24.253 --> 01:05:26.964
Now you know what they're really like.

01:05:27.172 --> 01:05:28.924
Britannia is rotten.

01:05:29.133 --> 01:05:32.928
If you want to change
the world, then join me!

01:05:33.137 --> 01:05:36.932
Did you... Is it true that
you killed Prince Clovis?

01:05:37.141 --> 01:05:38.517
This is war.

01:05:38.725 --> 01:05:41.812
It's only natural to kill an enemy commander.

01:05:42.020 --> 01:05:44.690
And the poison gas?
You took civilians hostage.

01:05:44.898 --> 01:05:49.319
Bluffing is essential to negotiation.
As a result, nobody was killed!

01:05:49.528 --> 01:05:51.321
Result?!

01:05:51.530 --> 01:05:55.367
So that's how you thought about it?

01:05:55.576 --> 01:05:57.369
Join me.

01:05:57.578 --> 01:05:59.997
Britannia is not a
nation worthy of your service.

01:06:00.205 --> 01:06:03.000
Maybe that's true. But...

01:06:03.208 --> 01:06:06.295
That's exactly why I'll change
it into a worthy nation!

01:06:06.503 --> 01:06:07.963
From within Britannia!

01:06:08.172 --> 01:06:09.214
Change it?

01:06:09.423 --> 01:06:13.594
Because I think the ends are worthless
if the means to them are wrong.

01:06:13.802 --> 01:06:15.387
Wait! Where are you going?!

01:06:15.596 --> 01:06:18.474
My court martial begins in an hour.

01:06:18.682 --> 01:06:19.808
Are you mad?!

01:06:20.017 --> 01:06:22.811
That trial is set up just to find you guilty!

01:06:23.020 --> 01:06:25.105
The prosecution, the judge, the defense!

01:06:25.314 --> 01:06:26.982
Even so, those are the rules.

01:06:27.191 --> 01:06:28.817
But you will die!

01:06:29.026 --> 01:06:29.526
That's fine.

01:06:29.735 --> 01:06:31.612
You're being stupid!

01:06:31.820 --> 01:06:36.742
An old friend used to tell me all
the time that I was being stupid.

01:06:36.950 --> 01:06:39.369
| guess it's a personal fault.

01:06:39.578 --> 01:06:43.207
| want to bring you in, but your group
would probably kill me if I tried now.

01:06:43.415 --> 01:06:47.211
If I'll be killed either way,
I'd rather it be for the sake of everyone.

01:06:47.419 --> 01:06:49.463
Even so... Thank you.

01:06:49.671 --> 01:06:51.882
For saving me.

01:06:53.967 --> 01:06:57.095
Yes, it seems the suspect,
Kururugi, contacted them.

01:06:57.304 --> 01:06:59.389
| suppose we can assume Zero released him.

01:06:59.598 --> 01:07:04.144
Still, now that the charges against him
have been thrown into question,

01:07:04.353 --> 01:07:07.439
it's possible that Private Kururugi
will be found innocent and acquitted...

01:07:07.648 --> 01:07:10.859
--Thank goodness.
--What would be the legal opinion on this?

01:07:11.068 --> 01:07:12.611
Miss Sayoko?

01:07:18.909 --> 01:07:19.743
I'm home.

01:07:19.952 --> 01:07:23.121
Welcome back, Lelouch.

01:07:23.330 --> 01:07:25.249
Welcome home, big brother!

01:07:25.457 --> 01:07:28.752
From your appearance,
can I assume you ate out tonight?

01:07:28.961 --> 01:07:30.295
| was worried!

01:07:30.504 --> 01:07:33.924
| thought you might be caught up
in the uproar that man Zero caused.

01:07:34.132 --> 01:07:38.345
| tried phoning you, but you didn't answer.

01:07:38.554 --> 01:07:42.724
Big brother? You're spacing out,
when Miss C.C. came to visit...

01:07:42.933 --> 01:07:44.935
<i>"C.C"?</i>

01:07:45.143 --> 01:07:48.730
What an odd friend you have.
Imagine, only going by her initials!

01:07:48.939 --> 01:07:49.773
Yeah...

01:07:49.982 --> 01:07:53.485
So, is she your girlfriend?

01:07:53.694 --> 01:07:56.071
We have promised our futures to each other.

01:07:56.280 --> 01:07:57.114
Right?

01:07:57.322 --> 01:07:59.825
"Futures"? You mean marriage?

01:08:00.033 --> 01:08:03.620
No! No, it's not like that.

01:08:03.829 --> 01:08:05.872
It's like, um... She's joking!

01:08:06.081 --> 01:08:07.791
| hate jokes.

01:08:08.959 --> 01:08:10.961
Who are you?!

01:08:11.169 --> 01:08:13.171
Didn't you hear her? My name is C.C.

01:08:13.380 --> 01:08:15.007
| don't mean your name! I thought...

01:08:15.215 --> 01:08:17.050
That I was dead?

01:08:18.427 --> 01:08:22.472
So, do you like the power that I gave you?

01:08:22.681 --> 01:08:24.850
As I thought. It was you.

01:08:25.058 --> 01:08:26.226
Dissatisfied?

01:08:26.435 --> 01:08:28.145
No, I'm grateful.

01:08:28.353 --> 01:08:31.815
It's allowed me to drastically
advance my schedule.

01:08:32.024 --> 01:08:33.734
Schedule?

01:08:33.942 --> 01:08:36.403
My schedule for obliterating Britannia.

01:08:36.612 --> 01:08:39.906
| had assumed I'd have to wait a
bit longer before I could make my move.

01:08:40.115 --> 01:08:43.910
You think you can destroy it?
Just with that power?

01:08:44.119 --> 01:08:47.539
I'd intended to do it without this power.

01:08:47.748 --> 01:08:50.792
| was right. This guy's fascinating...

01:08:51.001 --> 01:08:54.421
What will you do now?
The military must be after you.

01:08:54.630 --> 01:08:57.049
Only a tiny handful
of people know about me.

01:08:57.257 --> 01:08:59.801
So just hiding normally should be enough.

01:09:00.010 --> 01:09:01.637
I'll just have to make do here.

01:09:01.845 --> 01:09:03.805
Hey! You expect to sleep here?!

01:09:04.014 --> 01:09:05.390
Be a man and sleep on the floor.

01:09:05.599 --> 01:09:06.725
That's not what I meant!

01:09:06.933 --> 01:09:10.395
My being caught would be
trouble for you as well, correct?

01:09:10.604 --> 01:09:11.855
It's more dangerous for us to stay together!

01:09:12.064 --> 01:09:13.982
If I camp out in the open, I'll get arrested.

01:09:14.191 --> 01:09:16.526
This is about what's
convenient for me, not you!

01:09:16.735 --> 01:09:20.530
| hate stubbornness!

01:09:20.739 --> 01:09:22.699
You obviously aren't
bothered by much, are you?

01:09:22.908 --> 01:09:25.786
Anyway, how did you survive?
What's your story?

01:09:25.994 --> 01:09:28.163
And what about that contract you said--

01:09:28.372 --> 01:09:30.916
Good night, Lelouch.

01:09:32.876 --> 01:09:33.960
"Code-R"?

01:09:34.169 --> 01:09:36.963
Yes, what Prince Clovis and General Bartley

01:09:37.172 --> 01:09:39.591
were planning to present to the emperor.

01:09:39.800 --> 01:09:44.012
Ah, what they were transporting
under the guise of "poison gas."

01:09:44.221 --> 01:09:46.973
| wonder, why didn't
they present it right away?

01:09:47.182 --> 01:09:51.520
| was told that they wanted
to investigate a special power it had.

01:09:53.063 --> 01:09:54.314
Prince Schneizel?

01:09:54.523 --> 01:09:55.732
And what of Code-R?

01:09:55.941 --> 01:09:58.151
It apparently died during
the Shinjuku disturbance.

01:09:58.360 --> 01:10:02.197
So only General Bartley would know.

01:10:02.406 --> 01:10:06.034
So, what was that
"Orange" thing about, anyway?

01:10:08.370 --> 01:10:09.413
What?

01:10:09.621 --> 01:10:14.209
For somebody who won't answer
questions, you sure ask a lot of them.

01:10:14.418 --> 01:10:19.923
If you don't wish to answer them,
you don't have to. Just as I don't.

01:10:20.132 --> 01:10:22.259
Orange was just something I made up.

01:10:22.467 --> 01:10:25.762
However, groups who like
to use words like "comrades"

01:10:25.971 --> 01:10:29.683
are the easiest to split up by sowing suspicion.

01:10:33.603 --> 01:10:36.440
The whole world's looking for you.

01:10:36.648 --> 01:10:39.192
Because of you, the world is moving.

01:10:39.401 --> 01:10:42.696
Lelouch, is this what you wanted to see?

01:10:42.904 --> 01:10:46.116
No. This uproar is simply a means to an end.

01:10:46.324 --> 01:10:50.579
The world is destined for even greater chaos.

01:10:50.787 --> 01:10:55.876
Private Suzaku Kururugi, case number
107 of the Area 11 military forces.

01:10:56.084 --> 01:10:58.295
In the matter of the murder
of His Highness Prince Clovis,

01:10:58.503 --> 01:11:02.549
| hereby dismiss the charges
against you due to lack of evidence.

01:11:02.758 --> 01:11:04.593
Why the sudden about-face...?

01:11:04.801 --> 01:11:07.304
Out of the way, please!

01:11:07.512 --> 01:11:09.639
Look out below!

01:11:12.851 --> 01:11:14.478
Um, you aren't hurt, are you?

01:11:14.686 --> 01:11:18.064
Forgive me! |I didn't think
there was anyone below me!

01:11:18.273 --> 01:11:19.608
Um, that's okay.

01:11:19.816 --> 01:11:23.653
| wasn't expecting a girl
to come falling down on me, either.

01:11:23.862 --> 01:11:25.113
Oh, my!

01:11:25.322 --> 01:11:28.116
Is something wrong?

01:11:28.325 --> 01:11:30.577
Yes! Something is wrong!

01:11:31.703 --> 01:11:36.082
We're running late. I hope he's still waiting.

01:11:36.291 --> 01:11:38.585
But was he really released?

01:11:38.794 --> 01:11:40.504
For lack of evidence.

01:11:40.712 --> 01:11:43.590
Still, he was thoroughly questioned
about the incident with Zero-- Huh?

01:11:43.799 --> 01:11:45.383
Why's he...?

01:11:45.592 --> 01:11:46.885
Sir?

01:11:49.179 --> 01:11:53.225
| used my Geass to have
her mark the wall every day.

01:11:53.433 --> 01:11:54.559
Geass?

01:11:54.768 --> 01:11:59.523
This power. I thought I heard
that word when we made our contract.

01:11:59.731 --> 01:12:01.858
You're testing how long it lasts?

01:12:02.067 --> 01:12:04.402
| need to know the specs
of this weapon, don't 1?

01:12:04.611 --> 01:12:06.071
Don't act too selfish, or else...

01:12:06.279 --> 01:12:09.449
Do you think it would work on me?

01:12:09.658 --> 01:12:13.245
Relax. You and I are accomplices.

01:12:13.453 --> 01:12:16.414
| won't do anything to endanger us.

01:12:19.668 --> 01:12:22.587
To think I'd return to the homeland like this!

01:12:22.796 --> 01:12:26.842
| wish I'd never gotten
involved with the damned girl!

01:12:27.050 --> 01:12:31.221
To use my Geass, I have to have
direct eye contact with the subject.

01:12:31.429 --> 01:12:33.849
Effective range is approximately 270 meters.

01:12:34.057 --> 01:12:36.309
It can only be used once on any given person.

01:12:36.518 --> 01:12:38.687
It also appears that the subject
has no memory of events

01:12:38.895 --> 01:12:42.148
before, during, or after the power is used.

01:12:42.357 --> 01:12:47.779
| believe this is due to damage caused by the
Geass interfering with the subject's cerebrum.

01:12:47.988 --> 01:12:50.907
If it's an optical signal,
| should be able to reflect it.

01:12:51.116 --> 01:12:54.619
You've investigated it a lot
in the short time you've had it.

01:12:54.828 --> 01:12:58.123
My opponent is an empire which
controls over a third of the world.

01:12:58.331 --> 01:12:59.916
There's no such thing as being too careful.

01:13:00.125 --> 01:13:04.045
I'd understand if you were an Eleven,
but you're Britannian, aren't you?

01:13:04.254 --> 01:13:08.675
This opponent may be too large
and strong to fight with just a Geass.

01:13:08.884 --> 01:13:11.094
Does strong automatically mean good?

01:13:11.303 --> 01:13:13.847
Wait, Euphy's an imperial princess?!

01:13:14.055 --> 01:13:16.892
But... But she's got no guards!

01:13:17.100 --> 01:13:19.936
| think in this case, you're her guard.

01:13:20.145 --> 01:13:22.147
So, are you on a date?

01:13:22.355 --> 01:13:25.150
No, no! She just asked me
to stay with her, so I did.

01:13:25.358 --> 01:13:27.819
Suzaku, look! A kitty!

01:13:28.028 --> 01:13:29.571
Right, coming!

01:13:29.779 --> 01:13:31.656
Wow, he really didn't know.

01:13:31.865 --> 01:13:34.367
She was a student
until just recently, after all.

01:13:34.576 --> 01:13:38.246
If Princess Cornelia hadn't
been appointed the new viceroy,

01:13:38.455 --> 01:13:41.666
| doubt she'd have come here from Britannia.

01:13:41.875 --> 01:13:46.588
Euphy. In our position as blood sisters,
clear distinction is necessary.

01:13:46.796 --> 01:13:49.925
Henceforth, I will call you "Sub-Viceroy
Euphemia.” I trust you understand?

01:13:50.133 --> 01:13:52.302
Yes. I understand.

01:13:53.720 --> 01:13:55.889
Now then, your report?

01:13:56.097 --> 01:14:02.228
We have a welcome reception prepared
for Your Highness in the State building--

01:14:02.437 --> 01:14:07.567
Sloppy. Senile. Corrupt.

01:14:07.776 --> 01:14:11.237
What about Zero?!
Capture the enemy of the empire!

01:14:11.446 --> 01:14:13.114
Get Zero!

01:14:21.623 --> 01:14:24.960
Your Majesty, the remains have arrived.

01:14:25.168 --> 01:14:28.338
| was talking with Clovis just now.

01:14:28.546 --> 01:14:32.676
--Sire?
--The project must proceed. At once...

01:14:34.552 --> 01:14:39.349
I'll be joining you all here at
Ashford Academy starting today.

01:14:39.557 --> 01:14:41.226
I'm Suzaku Kururugi.

01:14:42.727 --> 01:14:43.770
Why's an Eleven here?

01:14:43.979 --> 01:14:46.231
He was a suspect in Prince Clovis's murder!

01:14:46.439 --> 01:14:48.066
But the teacher said his arrest was a mistake...

01:14:48.274 --> 01:14:50.902
But for them to arrest him, there must've
been something suspicious about him, right?

01:14:51.111 --> 01:14:54.322
You don't think he's a terrorist, do you?

01:14:54.531 --> 01:14:58.702
Of course not. The school
would've checked on that.

01:14:58.910 --> 01:14:59.869
An Eleven, here...

01:15:00.078 --> 01:15:01.830
He's an honorary Britannian.

01:15:02.038 --> 01:15:03.707
But that's the same thing.

01:15:03.915 --> 01:15:05.834
We shouldn't just be scared of him.

01:15:06.042 --> 01:15:08.753
If we talk to him, we can see what he's like!

01:15:08.962 --> 01:15:11.756
You gotta stop being such a woman of action.

01:15:40.785 --> 01:15:43.788
It's been seven years
since I last used that signal.

01:15:43.997 --> 01:15:45.832
"Let's talk in the attic," right?

01:15:46.041 --> 01:15:46.958
Yeah.

01:15:47.167 --> 01:15:49.794
I'm so glad you're okay.

01:15:50.003 --> 01:15:51.755
Thanks to you.

01:15:51.963 --> 01:15:55.050
But you had to go through all
that for protecting me...

01:15:55.258 --> 01:15:58.720
| was just returning the favor.
From seven years ago.

01:16:01.389 --> 01:16:03.975
What about that girl? The one in the capsule!

01:16:04.184 --> 01:16:06.978
We were separated during the fighting.

01:16:07.187 --> 01:16:08.980
Wouldn't you know more about her?

01:16:09.189 --> 01:16:13.985
No. It looks like only the
royal guard knew anything about her.

01:16:14.194 --> 01:16:15.653
Oh.

01:16:15.862 --> 01:16:18.865
So, your name--can
| still call you "Lelouch"?

01:16:19.074 --> 01:16:22.368
Since the records list my
former identity among the dead,

01:16:22.577 --> 01:16:25.538
| go by the name "Lelouch Lamperouge" now.

01:16:25.747 --> 01:16:26.831
Oh, I see.

01:16:27.040 --> 01:16:29.834
And you? What happened
at your court martial?

01:16:30.043 --> 01:16:31.753
And why did you enroll in this school?

01:16:31.961 --> 01:16:36.007
I'm just as surprised as you!
| had no idea you were here.

01:16:36.216 --> 01:16:41.471
And... Someone arranged for me
to get a proper investigation.

01:16:41.679 --> 01:16:45.183
They said that a
17-year-old should be in school.

01:16:54.442 --> 01:16:56.069
This hand...!

01:16:57.779 --> 01:16:59.155
Thank heaven.

01:16:59.364 --> 01:17:03.159
You really are all right!

01:17:03.368 --> 01:17:06.955
It's been a long time, Nunnally.

01:17:07.163 --> 01:17:09.874
You'll stay the night, won't you, Suzaku?

01:17:10.083 --> 01:17:12.836
Suzaku's a student at the school now.

01:17:13.044 --> 01:17:14.587
So you can visit him all the time now.

01:17:14.796 --> 01:17:15.630
Really?!

01:17:15.839 --> 01:17:19.717
| do have to work for the military
though, so it can't be every day.

01:17:19.926 --> 01:17:22.303
You're still in the military?

01:17:22.512 --> 01:17:23.555
It's all right.

01:17:23.763 --> 01:17:27.684
| got reassigned to an engineering
unit, so it's not that dangerous.

01:17:27.892 --> 01:17:31.437
| see. An engineering unit, huh?

01:17:31.646 --> 01:17:33.356
Wait, I'll help you.

01:17:33.565 --> 01:17:35.108
You just sit down.

01:17:35.316 --> 01:17:39.863
Unlike seven years ago, we're the hosts now.

01:17:40.071 --> 01:17:42.740
You've really mellowed since then.

01:17:42.949 --> 01:17:44.617
And you've gotten a lot rougher.

01:17:44.826 --> 01:17:46.411
Yeah, yeah.

01:17:49.038 --> 01:17:50.623
Didn't I tell you to stay in my room?

01:17:50.832 --> 01:17:55.837
That man is the Britannian soldier
from Shinjuku, isn't he? Is this wise?

01:17:56.045 --> 01:18:00.008
He's all right. He's...

01:18:00.216 --> 01:18:02.635
He's... my friend.

01:18:16.024 --> 01:18:18.109
And now an address by His Royal Majesty,

01:18:18.318 --> 01:18:23.156
the 98th emperor of
the Holy Britannian Empire.

01:18:27.076 --> 01:18:30.705
All men are not created equal.

01:18:30.914 --> 01:18:33.166
Some are born swifter.

01:18:33.374 --> 01:18:34.792
Some, more beautiful.

01:18:35.001 --> 01:18:36.878
Some are born to poor parents,

01:18:37.086 --> 01:18:39.255
while others are born sick and feeble!

01:18:39.464 --> 01:18:44.928
In birth, in upbringing,
in abilities, all humans are different.

01:18:45.136 --> 01:18:47.931
Yes, people exist precisely
to be discriminated among!

01:18:48.139 --> 01:18:53.519
And so they fight, they grow through
competition, and humanity progresses.

01:18:53.728 --> 01:18:56.481
Hatred, jealousy, inferiority complexes,
superiority complexes.

01:18:56.689 --> 01:18:59.484
All negative emotions are a form of energy.

01:18:59.692 --> 01:19:01.903
Inequality is not wrong!

01:19:02.111 --> 01:19:04.614
It is equality which is wrong!

01:19:04.822 --> 01:19:07.450
What of the E.U., which made equality a right?

01:19:07.659 --> 01:19:10.662
Mob rule by the most popular!

01:19:10.870 --> 01:19:12.914
And the Chinese, who equalized
the distribution of wealth?

01:19:13.122 --> 01:19:14.749
A nation of lazy dullards!

01:19:14.958 --> 01:19:17.961
But our beloved Britannia is different!

01:19:18.169 --> 01:19:22.048
We fight. We compete. We continuously evolve.

01:19:22.257 --> 01:19:27.345
Britannia alone moves forward,
advancing into the future!

01:19:27.553 --> 01:19:29.973
Even the death of my son, Clovis,

01:19:30.181 --> 01:19:33.726
is proof that Britannia continues to evolve.

01:19:33.935 --> 01:19:39.357
Fight on! Compete, steal,
acquire, and dominate!

01:19:39.565 --> 01:19:42.860
That is the path to our future!

01:19:43.069 --> 01:19:47.824
All hail Britannia!

01:19:49.158 --> 01:19:56.916
All hail Britannia! All hail Britannia!
All hail Britannia! All hail Britannia!

01:19:57.125 --> 01:19:59.043
All hail Britannia!

01:19:59.252 --> 01:20:02.255
All hail Britannia! All hail Britannia!

01:20:02.463 --> 01:20:05.258
So, this is Lelouch's enemy...

01:20:07.802 --> 01:20:10.555
All hail Britannia!

01:20:13.224 --> 01:20:16.269
What's wrong? Hurry inside!

01:20:16.477 --> 01:20:18.855
As of now, this is our hideout.

01:20:19.063 --> 01:20:22.233
Can I take that to mean
that you're teaming up with us?

01:20:22.442 --> 01:20:24.569
Yes. We're comrades, after all.

01:20:24.777 --> 01:20:26.154
Holy cow!

01:20:26.362 --> 01:20:28.906
What is this?

01:20:29.115 --> 01:20:31.534
How did you manage to get this?

01:20:31.743 --> 01:20:35.038
| asked a rather licentious nobleman
to let me have it for free.

01:20:35.246 --> 01:20:37.373
You asked for it? Just like that?

01:20:37.582 --> 01:20:39.834
Don't worry. It won't be traced to us.

01:20:41.085 --> 01:20:43.087
About the Orange incident--

01:20:43.296 --> 01:20:47.717
Pardon me. I meant the
Suzaku Kururugi incident.

01:20:47.925 --> 01:20:50.511
Is it true you can't remember anything?

01:20:50.720 --> 01:20:52.722
| don't expect you to believe me.

01:20:52.930 --> 01:20:56.017
No, it's just... I experienced
a blank in my memory

01:20:56.225 --> 01:20:58.186
during the Shinjuku incident, too.

01:20:58.394 --> 01:20:59.103
What?!

01:20:59.312 --> 01:21:03.316
When I regained my senses,
my Sutherland had been stolen.

01:21:03.524 --> 01:21:05.318
And right before the hole in my memory began,

01:21:05.526 --> 01:21:07.904
| ran into a boy wearing a student uniform.

01:21:08.112 --> 01:21:09.822
You think the student did it?

01:21:10.031 --> 01:21:14.619
| can't remember his face,
but it may be worth checking into.

01:21:25.421 --> 01:21:26.631
A Britannian...

01:21:26.839 --> 01:21:30.259
For a spy, he's certainly high-profile.
Is he an anti-nationalist?

01:21:30.468 --> 01:21:33.721
How wonderful that Zero
is attracting more subordinates.

01:21:33.930 --> 01:21:35.848
It was simpler than I thought it'd be.

01:21:36.057 --> 01:21:39.852
After all, the prevailing view among Elevens is,

01:21:40.061 --> 01:21:42.480
"While I hate the Britannians,
| can't approve of terrorism."

01:21:42.688 --> 01:21:46.776
Most Elevens will support
Zero's decisions, then?

01:21:46.984 --> 01:21:49.779
Which in turn makes it easier
for us to operate as a group.

01:21:49.987 --> 01:21:53.408
Even if all they do is decline to report us
to the authorities, that's still a big help.

01:21:53.616 --> 01:21:57.203
Some group called "Kyoto"
is offering to send us Knightmares, too.

01:21:57.412 --> 01:22:00.748
And our network of
informants is growing quickly.

01:22:00.957 --> 01:22:04.043
The Japanese can't resist a stampede.

01:22:04.252 --> 01:22:06.379
Give them any excuse to
agree with you, and away they go.

01:22:06.587 --> 01:22:08.923
Hence the big "Knights for Justice" act?

01:22:09.132 --> 01:22:13.010
Well, everyone likes heroic knights, don't they?

01:22:13.219 --> 01:22:16.514
That's not the facial expression
of a real Knight of Justice.

01:22:16.722 --> 01:22:17.807
You don't think so?

01:22:18.015 --> 01:22:22.770
| was demoted, just like you were.

01:22:22.979 --> 01:22:25.106
That's why we'd like to ask for your help.

01:22:25.314 --> 01:22:28.568
We have no intention of letting things end
like this, and we suspect you don't, either.

01:22:28.776 --> 01:22:30.319
Well, who can say?

01:22:30.528 --> 01:22:32.572
Don't you want to find Zero?

01:22:33.406 --> 01:22:35.408
Ashford Private Academy.

01:22:35.616 --> 01:22:37.743
We want you to check out
a male student there.

01:22:37.952 --> 01:22:40.204
We think he's working with Zero.

01:22:40.413 --> 01:22:45.626
We're going to the Narita mountains
for military duty. In the meantime...

01:22:45.835 --> 01:22:46.919
Narita?

01:22:47.128 --> 01:22:51.132
Isn't that where rumors say the
J.L.F.'s headquarters are located?

01:22:51.340 --> 01:22:53.801
You may be a bit too clever for your own good.

01:22:54.010 --> 01:22:56.053
You overestimate me.

01:22:58.598 --> 01:23:00.516
Lulu?

01:23:00.725 --> 01:23:01.893
Sheesh.

01:23:09.650 --> 01:23:10.818
Huh?

01:23:11.027 --> 01:23:13.863
Can I help you, miss?

01:23:14.071 --> 01:23:17.992
No, I'm sorry, I just thought
my friend was here!

01:23:19.660 --> 01:23:23.831
How weird... That was the third time.

01:23:26.626 --> 01:23:27.919
Incredible!

01:23:28.127 --> 01:23:29.295
These are Glasgows, right?

01:23:29.504 --> 01:23:31.881
They're a Japanese
customized version called a Burai.

01:23:32.089 --> 01:23:33.591
I've never seen these before!

01:23:33.799 --> 01:23:35.885
Man, this group has some serious power!

01:23:36.093 --> 01:23:38.012
It wasn't easy to join up with them.

01:23:38.221 --> 01:23:40.223
So, that makes us the elite, huh? The elite?!

01:23:40.431 --> 01:23:42.183
I'm getting fired up!

01:23:42.391 --> 01:23:44.769
Those Kyoto guys even sent us this?

01:23:44.977 --> 01:23:47.522
This thing is a completely
Japanese Knightmare!

01:23:47.730 --> 01:23:48.940
The Guren Mk-II.

01:23:49.148 --> 01:23:50.358
Did you check out the manual?

01:23:50.566 --> 01:23:53.903
The radiant wave surger?
It's an incredible weapon!

01:23:54.111 --> 01:23:55.363
| love it!

01:23:55.571 --> 01:23:59.283
The big shots in Kyoto are
recognizing us Black Knights!

01:23:59.492 --> 01:24:00.952
--Sir!
--Yeah?

01:24:01.160 --> 01:24:03.037
| was wondering how
to use this equipment...

01:24:03.246 --> 01:24:05.206
Oh, hang on! I'll be right over there!

01:24:05.414 --> 01:24:07.875
Newbies. What are you gonna do?

01:24:10.545 --> 01:24:11.712
| expect it from Tamaki,

01:24:11.921 --> 01:24:14.423
but now Inoue and the others
are acting like this is a party, too?

01:24:14.632 --> 01:24:18.219
Kyoto is backing multiple
resistance groups, isn't it?

01:24:18.427 --> 01:24:21.305
Yes, which means we've finally made it in.

01:24:21.514 --> 01:24:23.891
No, you're wrong there, Kallen.

01:24:24.100 --> 01:24:25.685
This is merely a test for us.

01:24:25.893 --> 01:24:28.688
Even just them wanting
to test us is incredible!

01:24:28.896 --> 01:24:30.481
You're an optimist.

01:24:33.317 --> 01:24:34.151
What's...?

01:24:34.360 --> 01:24:36.654
The Guren Mk-Il is yours now, Kallen.

01:24:36.862 --> 01:24:39.699
Mine?! But we have a lot more people now!

01:24:39.907 --> 01:24:42.326
With the Guren's defenses,
you should be the one...

01:24:42.535 --> 01:24:44.036
You're an ace pilot.

01:24:44.245 --> 01:24:46.622
I'm a commander. I'll use a Burai,

01:24:46.831 --> 01:24:49.417
but you're our only ace
to play during a battle.

01:24:50.793 --> 01:24:51.752
Yes, sir.

01:24:51.961 --> 01:24:54.088
Zero, you got a second?

01:24:54.297 --> 01:24:59.176
We've got some weird intel here.
It's from that Britannian applicant.

01:24:59.385 --> 01:25:02.305
It may be a trap to draw us out.

01:25:02.513 --> 01:25:06.684
It'd be hard to confirm for certain,
because contacting him is risky...

01:25:06.892 --> 01:25:11.188
But this news is too big to ignore.
What should we do?

01:25:11.397 --> 01:25:13.024
Perhaps we'll take a
hiking trip this weekend.

01:25:13.232 --> 01:25:13.983
Pardon?

01:25:14.191 --> 01:25:16.152
To the Narita mountains.

01:25:19.280 --> 01:25:20.990
Sector 5, nothing to report.

01:25:21.198 --> 01:25:24.660
Right, the next scheduled report
will be in two hours.

01:25:24.869 --> 01:25:26.746
Of course there's nothing to report!

01:25:26.954 --> 01:25:32.543
This area's totally under the Japan Liberation
Front's control. No one can just...

01:25:32.752 --> 01:25:33.419
--Zero!
--Zero?!

01:25:33.628 --> 01:25:36.422
Relax, I just came to talk.

01:25:36.631 --> 01:25:40.384
All you have to do is ignore
all unusual activity out here.

01:25:45.848 --> 01:25:46.974
Sure, no problem!

01:25:47.183 --> 01:25:48.392
Come on, it's your turn!

01:25:48.601 --> 01:25:52.063
Don't be in such a rush!
We're supposedly on duty, you know!

01:25:55.941 --> 01:26:00.071
I've confirmed the signal from Zero.
We're now moving to Site 2.

01:26:02.114 --> 01:26:03.491
This is military training, right?

01:26:03.699 --> 01:26:05.576
With Zero in another
location from the rest of us?

01:26:05.785 --> 01:26:07.161
Maybe we'll dig a hot spring.

01:26:07.370 --> 01:26:10.539
Is that why we brought those excavators?
Hell, I'm all for it then.

01:26:10.539 --> 01:26:10.665
“"Narita Mountains”™ [ ] I HQII Is that why we
brought those excavators? Hell, I'm all for it then.

01:26:10.665 --> 01:26:12.416
"Narita Mountains"
n HQII

01:26:12.667 --> 01:26:15.670
Cornelia, at last, this day has come.

01:26:19.423 --> 01:26:23.678
We're certain that the Japan Liberation Front's
headquarters are in this area.

01:26:23.886 --> 01:26:26.889
We've already split four battalions
into seven units and hidden them.

01:26:27.098 --> 01:26:28.891
As soon as we receive the viceroy's signal,

01:26:29.100 --> 01:26:31.268
we'll tighten the encirclement
around them and wipe them out.

01:26:31.477 --> 01:26:35.606
No enemies will appear from outside
of the encirclement, will they?

01:26:35.815 --> 01:26:36.732
You mean Zero?

01:26:36.941 --> 01:26:38.275
Have no fear.

01:26:38.484 --> 01:26:40.736
As the operation starts, we'll block off

01:26:40.945 --> 01:26:42.697
the surrounding highways and roads.

01:26:42.905 --> 01:26:43.989
And we have reserve units.

01:26:44.198 --> 01:26:48.661
If Zero is stupid enough to show up,
that'll be the end for him.

01:26:48.869 --> 01:26:51.580
C.C., what are you doing here?!

01:26:51.789 --> 01:26:53.582
| said that I'd protect you, didn't I?

01:26:53.791 --> 01:26:55.376
Oh, so now you're my guardian?

01:26:55.584 --> 01:26:58.754
Lelouch, Lelouch!
Wherefore art thou Lelouch?

01:26:58.963 --> 01:27:01.382
| don't have time to discuss philosophy.

01:27:01.590 --> 01:27:03.968
You changed your
family name to Lamperouge,

01:27:04.176 --> 01:27:07.888
but kept Lelouch as your personal name.

01:27:08.097 --> 01:27:10.349
How soft. You can't let go of the past.

01:27:10.558 --> 01:27:14.895
Well, "C.C." is going too far
the other way. It's not a human name.

01:27:20.693 --> 01:27:26.073
Lelouch, do you know why snow is white?

01:27:26.282 --> 01:27:30.327
Because it's forgotten
what color it's supposed to be.

01:27:30.536 --> 01:27:32.121
Viceroy, it's time.

01:27:32.329 --> 01:27:34.832
Very well. Commence operation!

01:27:36.709 --> 01:27:39.754
Japan Liberation Front...

01:27:39.962 --> 01:27:44.925
You who were left behind by time, who
forgot the benevolence bestowed on you...

01:27:45.134 --> 01:27:49.054
Now you and your dream
of a great nation shall crumble!

01:27:52.266 --> 01:27:53.392
An enemy attack?!

01:27:53.601 --> 01:27:56.687
The Britannian forces have the
Narita mountains completely encircled!

01:27:56.896 --> 01:27:58.856
There are over 100 of them!

01:28:00.983 --> 01:28:02.818
It's begun.

01:28:03.027 --> 01:28:06.614
You've got... You've gotta be kidding, Zero!

01:28:06.822 --> 01:28:10.034
Those guys will have us totally surrounded!
And our way out...

01:28:10.242 --> 01:28:12.036
...has doubtless been cut off.

01:28:12.244 --> 01:28:15.039
The only way to survive now is to wage war.

01:28:15.247 --> 01:28:17.625
War? With the Britannians?

01:28:17.833 --> 01:28:20.544
Fight them head on?!
Even though we're surrounded?!

01:28:20.753 --> 01:28:22.630
Not to mention those are Cornelia's forces!

01:28:22.838 --> 01:28:24.757
They're way stronger than
anyone we've been fighting so far!

01:28:24.965 --> 01:28:27.301
Correct. It'll be a miracle if we win this.

01:28:27.510 --> 01:28:28.928
Zero, what are you saying?!

01:28:29.136 --> 01:28:32.556
Even the Messiah needs to
perform miracles to be acknowledged!

01:28:32.765 --> 01:28:35.643
Which means we have to produce
a miracle of our own, don't we?

01:28:35.851 --> 01:28:39.522
Now look, miracles don't come cheap!

01:28:39.730 --> 01:28:43.400
| knew it was nuts to make
you our leader! It should be me!

01:28:48.781 --> 01:28:50.282
Our retreat has already been cut off.

01:28:50.491 --> 01:28:55.412
If you think you can win without me,
then someone shoot me. Anyone!

01:29:00.793 --> 01:29:04.630
If you look up to me as leader,
you have just two choices.

01:29:04.839 --> 01:29:08.300
Either live with me, or die with me!

01:29:08.509 --> 01:29:10.594
The main enemy force should
be coming out any time now.

01:29:10.803 --> 01:29:12.721
We're switching to E.C.C.M. mode.

01:29:12.930 --> 01:29:15.057
Link up on channel alpha-four!

01:29:15.266 --> 01:29:17.351
The enemy's... What are they called again?

01:29:17.560 --> 01:29:18.435
The Burais, sir?

01:29:18.644 --> 01:29:21.313
Right. Just watch out
for those Glasgow rip-offs!

01:29:21.522 --> 01:29:23.357
Yes, my lord!

01:29:26.694 --> 01:29:29.280
So, they turned this
whole mountain into a fortress.

01:29:29.488 --> 01:29:30.823
Your Highness, please fall back!

01:29:31.031 --> 01:29:34.869
Guilford, don't treat me
like any ordinary woman.

01:29:35.953 --> 01:29:36.912
Princess Cornelia!

01:29:37.121 --> 01:29:38.455
It can't be! Cornelia?!

01:29:38.664 --> 01:29:40.624
Don't panic! We'll take out their leader!

01:29:40.833 --> 01:29:42.751
Insolent worms!

01:29:51.051 --> 01:29:54.638
Oh, well then. I'll cover you from the rear.

01:29:54.847 --> 01:29:59.059
Well?! Cornelia is here!
Is there no one who will challenge me?!

01:29:59.268 --> 01:30:02.396
What's wrong? Challenge me
and try to take me down!

01:30:03.397 --> 01:30:04.982
Fine! Do what you want!

01:30:05.190 --> 01:30:07.484
Right. You're our leader.

01:30:07.693 --> 01:30:10.112
Thank you. I appreciate it.

01:30:13.115 --> 01:30:14.241
Too fragile.

01:30:14.450 --> 01:30:18.370
The enemy seems to be concentrated
over here. We may have hit the jackpot!

01:30:18.579 --> 01:30:19.997
Split up!

01:30:22.791 --> 01:30:25.961
No good! Our second
attack wave has had no effect!

01:30:27.671 --> 01:30:29.840
Is that Darlton?

01:30:30.049 --> 01:30:32.051
So, that's where the main enemy base is?

01:30:32.259 --> 01:30:34.511
All right, we'll hold this position.

01:30:34.720 --> 01:30:36.096
Are you sure that's wise?

01:30:36.305 --> 01:30:39.016
I've no interest in stealing
achievements from my subordinates.

01:30:39.224 --> 01:30:43.228
Send the reserve force to back up to Darlton!
Looks like he'll be getting another medal.

01:30:44.438 --> 01:30:47.650
Impressive as always, Cornelia.
A very logical deployment.

01:30:52.738 --> 01:30:55.616
Weren't the reserve units
supposed go to General Darlton?

01:30:55.824 --> 01:30:59.620
Yes, but our unit's orders are
to secure Viceroy Cornelia's rear line.

01:30:59.828 --> 01:31:03.040
This is the rear line?! That's the furthest
you can get from the main battlefield!

01:31:03.248 --> 01:31:06.961
How am I supposed to clear my name here?!

01:31:08.420 --> 01:31:09.797
Contact lost with Kohashi's unit!

01:31:10.005 --> 01:31:11.715
No response from sector 3!

01:31:11.924 --> 01:31:13.050
Major Tamata's been killed!

01:31:13.258 --> 01:31:14.718
Kuroda and Kurata are also gone!

01:31:14.927 --> 01:31:16.553
What about Sakamoto?!

01:31:16.762 --> 01:31:20.683
If only... If only Tohdoh were here,
then the divine wind would blow!

01:31:20.891 --> 01:31:23.936
We'd have another Miracle of Itsukushimal!

01:31:26.397 --> 01:31:28.357
Don't you think you're going
a little overboard, Tohdoh?

01:31:28.565 --> 01:31:31.694
Asahina, Chiba! Prep the
Burai Customs for deployment!

01:31:31.902 --> 01:31:33.862
Tell Urabe and Senba behind us to do the same.

01:31:34.071 --> 01:31:36.073
They've blocked traffic all around Narita.

01:31:36.281 --> 01:31:38.534
It's already begun!

01:31:45.416 --> 01:31:48.210
With this, the resistance's
strength in Area 11...

01:31:48.419 --> 01:31:49.628
...is finished.

01:31:49.837 --> 01:31:52.381
Right! All preparations are complete!

01:31:52.589 --> 01:31:55.843
All Black Knights, prepare to move out!

01:31:56.051 --> 01:31:57.344
Dammit, we have no choice!

01:31:57.553 --> 01:31:58.512
| ain't gonna die!

01:31:58.721 --> 01:32:00.055
We'll make a miracle happen!

01:32:00.264 --> 01:32:01.890
We have Zero with us!

01:32:02.099 --> 01:32:03.934
The Black Knights will now launch

01:32:04.143 --> 01:32:07.229
a surprise attack on the Britannians
from the mountain summit!

01:32:07.438 --> 01:32:11.233
On my orders, charge down on point 3!

01:32:11.442 --> 01:32:15.863
The operation's objective is the capture
of Cornelia, second princess of Britannia!

01:32:16.071 --> 01:32:19.241
The Guren Mk-II will cut us a path!

01:32:20.367 --> 01:32:22.995
Kallen! Use penetrating electrode number 3!

01:32:23.203 --> 01:32:24.705
| assume you can do this in one blow, correct?

01:32:24.913 --> 01:32:26.623
Yes, sir.

01:32:27.750 --> 01:32:31.670
Output confirmed. Radiant wave
surger maintaining level status.

01:32:36.383 --> 01:32:38.427
Induction!

01:32:53.859 --> 01:32:55.694
It worked!

01:33:07.748 --> 01:33:08.332
What's happening?!

01:33:08.540 --> 01:33:09.124
An earthquake?!

01:33:09.333 --> 01:33:11.085
At a time like this?!

01:33:11.293 --> 01:33:12.377
What?!

01:33:13.378 --> 01:33:14.296
What's...?

01:33:14.505 --> 01:33:17.007
A giant landslide like this... Impossible!

01:33:17.216 --> 01:33:19.927
Alex's and Darlton's units will be wiped out!

01:33:20.135 --> 01:33:22.429
Climb! Get to higher ground!

01:33:22.638 --> 01:33:23.639
Sit-rep?

01:33:23.847 --> 01:33:24.723
We're still trying to confirm.

01:33:24.932 --> 01:33:27.392
Your Highness, pull back!
You're in danger there!

01:33:32.773 --> 01:33:36.068
Oh-ho. It's even more
destructive than I anticipated.

01:33:36.276 --> 01:33:40.864
We did succeed in isolating Cornelia's unit,
but perhaps it needs more precision.

01:33:41.073 --> 01:33:42.324
I'll have to consult my physics teacher--

01:33:42.533 --> 01:33:46.328
No, I should ask Nina.
She'll toss in probability theory.

01:33:46.537 --> 01:33:48.664
New enemy force
approaching from the summit.

01:33:48.872 --> 01:33:51.083
Carius's unit is moving to engage them.

01:33:51.291 --> 01:33:55.003
It's not the Japan Liberation Front.
| believe it's Zero's group!

01:33:55.212 --> 01:33:56.547
What?! Then...

01:33:56.755 --> 01:33:57.631
It's Zero!

01:33:57.840 --> 01:33:59.842
How good of you to come, Zero!

01:34:00.050 --> 01:34:02.302
Lord Jeremiah! You can't
just abandon your position!

01:34:02.511 --> 01:34:06.473
It's an emergency! If you want
glory in life, then follow me!

01:34:06.682 --> 01:34:08.475
Cornelia only has limited
reinforcements headed her way.

01:34:08.684 --> 01:34:09.726
Break right through them!

01:34:09.935 --> 01:34:12.479
Sure! Let's do this thing!

01:34:14.439 --> 01:34:18.110
Our duty is to guard their backs, understood?!

01:34:18.318 --> 01:34:19.403
Fire!

01:34:22.573 --> 01:34:24.867
Carius's unit has been wiped out?!

01:34:25.075 --> 01:34:28.704
If I can settle this before Zero
reaches Princess Cornelia, then...

01:34:28.912 --> 01:34:29.955
Lord Jeremiah.

01:34:30.164 --> 01:34:32.791
Villetta? So you came!

01:34:33.000 --> 01:34:35.085
Burning bridges and downhill rushes...

01:34:35.294 --> 01:34:38.130
Who'd have thought classical
strategies would prove so effective?

01:34:38.338 --> 01:34:39.798
Zero!

01:34:40.007 --> 01:34:41.091
Dammit!

01:34:43.343 --> 01:34:46.054
Are you here, Zero?!
If you are, then face me!

01:34:46.263 --> 01:34:48.348
Fight Jeremiah Gottwald!

01:34:48.557 --> 01:34:53.061
Well, now... It's been a while, hasn't it?
You're still in the army?

01:34:53.270 --> 01:34:57.858
However, I don't have time to play
with you now, my dear Orange.

01:34:58.066 --> 01:35:00.652
O...! Ora...!

01:35:00.861 --> 01:35:02.487
Orange, huh?!

01:35:02.696 --> 01:35:04.656
Diel!

01:35:09.411 --> 01:35:10.370
Lord Jeremiah!

01:35:10.579 --> 01:35:13.040
Stay out of this! This is my duel!

01:35:13.248 --> 01:35:16.501
But I've never seen
a Knightmare like that before.

01:35:16.710 --> 01:35:17.961
Could the Elevens have--

01:35:18.170 --> 01:35:21.340
As though Elevens could manage
that sort of technology!

01:35:23.967 --> 01:35:25.052
It's fast!

01:35:28.138 --> 01:35:30.474
This thing... This is what
destroyed Carius's unit?!

01:35:30.682 --> 01:35:35.229
You see, Britannia?!
At last, we can fight you head on!

01:35:35.437 --> 01:35:39.566
With this Guren Mk-II,
our counterattack begins!

01:35:39.775 --> 01:35:42.611
Oh, hell... There's some
kind of trick to its right hand!

01:35:42.819 --> 01:35:45.322
But, if I keep my distance...

01:35:45.530 --> 01:35:46.615
What?!

01:35:51.662 --> 01:35:52.788
Forgive me.

01:36:03.590 --> 01:36:05.550
Wh-What's happening?!

01:36:05.759 --> 01:36:06.927
Lord Jeremiah, eject!

01:36:07.135 --> 01:36:12.933
How can I?! Zero is right in front of me!
Zero is right here!

01:36:13.141 --> 01:36:16.061
Dammit! The auto-eject?!
Don't you dare activate!

01:36:16.270 --> 01:36:18.814
| can still... I can still get Zero!

01:36:30.325 --> 01:36:33.078
It took down Jeremiah...?

01:36:33.287 --> 01:36:35.497
All conditions have been cleared.

01:36:35.706 --> 01:36:36.832
The pieces are in place.

01:36:37.040 --> 01:36:40.210
All that's left is to check
my opponent's stronghold.

01:36:42.254 --> 01:36:43.380
What do our losses look like?!

01:36:43.588 --> 01:36:45.799
| only read signals from
20 percent of our forces.

01:36:46.008 --> 01:36:47.175
20 percent?!

01:36:47.384 --> 01:36:49.720
Our command structure can't hold up like this!

01:36:49.928 --> 01:36:52.973
This is Marceau unit.
| can't raise General Alex!

01:36:53.181 --> 01:36:55.183
It looks like the second division
has been wiped out!

01:36:55.392 --> 01:36:57.019
Mr. Lloyd, what's going on?!

01:36:57.227 --> 01:37:01.231
It's unconfirmed, but there are reports
that Zero's group has appeared.

01:37:01.440 --> 01:37:02.566
Zero?

01:37:04.943 --> 01:37:06.153
Is the viceroy all right?

01:37:06.361 --> 01:37:08.155
She was outside the slide path,
so that's no problem.

01:37:08.363 --> 01:37:11.992
But since the units guarding her rear moved,
she's practically isolated...

01:37:12.200 --> 01:37:14.745
What the hell is Orange doing?!

01:37:14.953 --> 01:37:16.872
All right, Guren, head to
your designated position!

01:37:17.080 --> 01:37:19.416
The remaining force here
will go after Cornelia!

01:37:19.624 --> 01:37:20.292
--Right!
--Gotcha!

01:37:20.500 --> 01:37:21.918
We're gonna pull this off!

01:37:22.127 --> 01:37:23.462
Defend this position at all costs!

01:37:26.757 --> 01:37:28.550
Sugiyama! You okay?!

01:37:28.759 --> 01:37:30.302
Y-Yeah...

01:37:34.306 --> 01:37:35.640
Dammit! Get them!

01:37:35.849 --> 01:37:37.476
The Purebloods are holding them off?

01:37:37.684 --> 01:37:39.102
Yes, sir! Under Lady Villetta's command.

01:37:39.311 --> 01:37:42.230
Then this is our chance!
Get the viceroy to fall back!

01:37:42.439 --> 01:37:43.148
Send in air support!

01:37:43.357 --> 01:37:47.027
Wait! Something's approaching
the viceroy from behind!

01:37:47.235 --> 01:37:49.154
All units, are you ready?

01:37:49.363 --> 01:37:51.782
--Yes, sir!
--All right. Deploy the Burai Customs.

01:37:51.990 --> 01:37:53.742
Moving out!

01:37:53.950 --> 01:37:56.495
Am I clear? If this landslide was manmade,

01:37:56.703 --> 01:37:59.748
| think we can take Cornelia from behind.

01:37:59.956 --> 01:38:01.500
Capture Cornelia!

01:38:01.708 --> 01:38:04.086
Right now, we'll pay them back
for what happened seven years ago!

01:38:04.294 --> 01:38:07.547
Yes, sir! By the honor
of the Four Holy Swords!

01:38:07.756 --> 01:38:09.049
What?!

01:38:09.257 --> 01:38:10.884
Protect Her Highness!

01:38:15.180 --> 01:38:16.348
Surround them!

01:38:16.556 --> 01:38:18.975
The Japan Liberation Front?

01:38:19.184 --> 01:38:20.394
Slash and Encircle formation.

01:38:20.602 --> 01:38:21.686
Wilco!

01:38:23.647 --> 01:38:25.690
Don't assume these are just any Burais.

01:38:25.899 --> 01:38:27.692
This reminds me of seven years ago.

01:38:27.901 --> 01:38:31.780
It's different now.
This time, we have Knightmares, too!

01:38:31.988 --> 01:38:35.492
Your Highness, leave them to us!
Please, withdraw for now!

01:38:36.993 --> 01:38:39.413
In that case, I'll go turn the tables on them.

01:38:39.621 --> 01:38:40.914
--Guilford.
--Highness?

01:38:41.123 --> 01:38:43.875
Once you fend them off, meet me at point 9.

01:38:44.084 --> 01:38:45.293
Point 9?

01:38:45.502 --> 01:38:46.378
Understood!

01:38:46.586 --> 01:38:49.131
All right, keep this up and nail down Zero!

01:38:49.339 --> 01:38:51.883
C'mon, maybe we should ask
for Kallen to get back here!

01:38:52.092 --> 01:38:55.262
We can't! If we change our positioning,
the plan falls apart!

01:38:55.470 --> 01:38:56.930
Still, this doesn't look good.

01:38:57.139 --> 01:38:59.933
If this keeps up,
we may have to take on her royal guard.

01:39:00.142 --> 01:39:02.769
Zero! They're saying Cornelia's
under attack from below!

01:39:02.978 --> 01:39:04.563
What? Which team made the move?

01:39:04.771 --> 01:39:07.858
Not one of ours. Looks like it's the J.L.F.

01:39:08.066 --> 01:39:10.068
Did one of them figure out what I'm after?

01:39:10.277 --> 01:39:11.153
Clever.

01:39:11.361 --> 01:39:14.114
Then they'll hold off the royal guard for us!

01:39:14.322 --> 01:39:16.408
Sorry we're late, General!

01:39:16.616 --> 01:39:18.368
Tohdoh! We've been waiting for you!

01:39:18.577 --> 01:39:21.538
Sir, please send all the forces
you have to my position.

01:39:21.746 --> 01:39:23.206
Can we still beat them?

01:39:23.415 --> 01:39:25.792
If we can hold off the main
Britannian force, we can!

01:39:26.001 --> 01:39:27.919
Now is our chance!

01:39:29.963 --> 01:39:31.882
Dammit! And at a time like this!

01:39:32.090 --> 01:39:32.883
What do we do, sir?!

01:39:33.091 --> 01:39:36.845
Change course! Whatever it takes,
we have to rendezvous with Princess Cornelia!

01:39:37.053 --> 01:39:38.889
But sir, the enemy's main base
is right in front of us!

01:39:39.097 --> 01:39:41.892
And if we take an attack from behind,
the damage will be enormous!

01:39:42.100 --> 01:39:46.354
You fool! If the princess is lost,
the battle's all over!

01:39:46.563 --> 01:39:48.190
Y-Yes, sir--

01:39:51.318 --> 01:39:53.320
Dammit, you're good.

01:39:54.779 --> 01:39:55.864
Scatter!

01:39:57.407 --> 01:39:59.701
Colonel! What about Cornelia?

01:39:59.910 --> 01:40:02.829
If Zero's the man I think he is,
he's got a plan in play!

01:40:03.038 --> 01:40:05.290
All we can do now is trust him!

01:40:05.499 --> 01:40:07.209
What? Zero has changed course?!

01:40:07.417 --> 01:40:10.712
Yes. We're en route to give you support.

01:40:10.921 --> 01:40:13.256
Zero comes first! Give me his location!

01:40:13.465 --> 01:40:16.885
Y-Yes, sir! This is Zero's projected course.

01:40:17.093 --> 01:40:17.969
Oh, hell!

01:40:18.178 --> 01:40:21.473
Zero's group is headed to where she
intends to lead Tohdoh and the others!

01:40:21.681 --> 01:40:23.266
Princess Cornelia!

01:40:24.726 --> 01:40:27.395
| can hear you, Guilford.

01:40:28.563 --> 01:40:32.359
Sub-Viceroy Euphemia, we must charge in
with G1 and save the viceroy!

01:40:32.567 --> 01:40:33.193
No!

01:40:33.401 --> 01:40:37.989
<i>But, with even Commander Guilford pinned
down, Viceroy Cornelia's life is in danger!</i>

01:40:38.198 --> 01:40:39.241
We mustn't!

01:40:39.449 --> 01:40:42.327
There's a field hospital set up here!

01:40:42.536 --> 01:40:45.163
Not to mention civilians who
have evacuated from the area!

01:40:45.372 --> 01:40:48.583
What's more, this G1 base
represents our headquarters!

01:40:48.792 --> 01:40:51.419
The viceroy specifically ordered
me not to move it, no matter what!

01:40:51.628 --> 01:40:53.880
That's why... Why...

01:40:55.215 --> 01:40:59.386
Hi there! Advanced Special Envoy
Engineering Corps, at your service!

01:40:59.594 --> 01:41:00.387
How dare you!

01:41:00.595 --> 01:41:03.598
You irregulars should be quiet
and stick to observing!

01:41:03.807 --> 01:41:05.976
Um, you make a good point, sir, but...

01:41:06.184 --> 01:41:08.979
But all this waiting around is getting to us.

01:41:10.272 --> 01:41:11.773
Sub-Viceroy Euphemia.

01:41:11.982 --> 01:41:15.485
| beg of you, please order us into combat.

01:41:15.694 --> 01:41:16.903
Cornelia!!

01:41:17.112 --> 01:41:18.780
Lowborn scum!

01:41:22.284 --> 01:41:25.495
What the... That's not just
a customized machine, is it?

01:41:29.165 --> 01:41:31.668
Are you listening, Cornelia?

01:41:31.876 --> 01:41:33.253
This is already a checkmate.

01:41:33.461 --> 01:41:35.130
--Is that you, Zero?
--Yes.

01:41:35.338 --> 01:41:37.340
Perhaps we should celebrate our meeting.

01:41:37.549 --> 01:41:41.386
However, before we do,
I'd like you to please surrender to us.

01:41:41.595 --> 01:41:44.055
There are some things
I'd like to ask you, as well.

01:41:45.098 --> 01:41:47.392
Incidentally, your reinforcements
won't make it here in time.

01:41:47.601 --> 01:41:50.478
| win, Cornelia.

01:41:51.980 --> 01:41:53.523
Don't be a fool, Zero.

01:41:53.732 --> 01:41:54.941
This one...

01:41:55.150 --> 01:41:57.819
If I just destroy this one,
| open my path of escape!

01:42:01.531 --> 01:42:03.241
You're a clever one!

01:42:14.002 --> 01:42:16.338
You dishonorable--
You'd shoot me from behind?!

01:42:16.546 --> 01:42:20.717
Oh? You're saying your own plan
wasn't dishonorable at heart?

01:42:24.220 --> 01:42:26.806
They launched a pincer attack
before we could regroup!

01:42:27.015 --> 01:42:29.601
There's no way I'll reach Her Highness now!

01:42:35.315 --> 01:42:37.692
Colonel, we've eliminated
the enemy reinforcements!

01:42:37.901 --> 01:42:40.904
All right! Switch to
Rotating Absolute Power formation!

01:42:41.112 --> 01:42:42.197
Wilco!

01:42:44.032 --> 01:42:46.034
At this rate, Princess Cornelia will be...

01:42:46.242 --> 01:42:48.078
Guilford.

01:42:48.286 --> 01:42:50.497
Guilford, my knight...

01:42:50.705 --> 01:42:53.166
| want you and Darlton to assist Euphy.

01:42:53.375 --> 01:42:54.209
Your Highness!

01:42:54.417 --> 01:42:56.753
| refuse to surrender.

01:42:56.961 --> 01:42:59.923
As an imperial princess,
| will fight to my last breath!

01:43:00.131 --> 01:43:02.092
Princess Cornelia!

01:43:03.426 --> 01:43:05.178
What a foolish choice.

01:43:14.312 --> 01:43:16.272
As reckless as ever, I see.

01:43:16.481 --> 01:43:19.609
Using the V.A.R.L.S. to clear
the obstacles in his path...

01:43:22.987 --> 01:43:26.408
Your Highness, are you all right?
I've come to help.

01:43:26.616 --> 01:43:28.785
A.S.E.E.C.? But who authorized you?

01:43:28.993 --> 01:43:31.037
Hey, isn't that Knightmare...?

01:43:31.246 --> 01:43:33.331
Yeah, it's Britannia's new model!

01:43:33.540 --> 01:43:36.418
Again... He's interfering again!

01:43:39.337 --> 01:43:41.548
Guren Mk-Il, destroy the White Helmet!

01:43:41.756 --> 01:43:43.299
That thing's breakthrough power is a nuisance!

01:43:43.508 --> 01:43:44.592
Right!

01:43:52.016 --> 01:43:54.894
You handle that thing! I'll take out Zero!

01:43:57.230 --> 01:43:59.107
Here's where you pay for Shinjuku!

01:44:02.068 --> 01:44:04.487
Is this possible?! It's as fast as Lancelot!

01:44:06.865 --> 01:44:08.575
If I can just take down this thing...

01:44:17.333 --> 01:44:19.127
That weapon won't work!

01:44:28.344 --> 01:44:29.596
It stopped it?!

01:44:39.939 --> 01:44:41.274
Hey! Are you okay?

01:44:41.483 --> 01:44:42.525
Y-Yeah.

01:44:42.734 --> 01:44:44.360
Ohgi! How's the Guren?!

01:44:44.569 --> 01:44:46.863
The right hand's busted. We need to repair it.

01:44:48.990 --> 01:44:50.074
Retreat!

01:44:50.283 --> 01:44:52.660
All units, move to the escape point!

01:44:52.869 --> 01:44:55.497
At this rate, it'll turn into
a war of attrition. Retreat!

01:44:59.250 --> 01:44:59.876
Your Highness!

01:45:00.084 --> 01:45:01.377
Go after Zero!

01:45:01.586 --> 01:45:04.422
--But...
--My energy filler's just drained! Now go!

01:45:04.631 --> 01:45:05.965
R-Right!

01:45:08.301 --> 01:45:10.637
Hey, should we really just quit like this?

01:45:10.845 --> 01:45:13.598
We've definitely won here,
but we're at our limit.

01:45:13.807 --> 01:45:17.602
In other words, all we can do is let
the J.L.F. play decoy while we run?

01:45:17.811 --> 01:45:20.188
| hate that choice of words, but...

01:45:20.396 --> 01:45:24.526
Yeah. People aren't just chess pawns.

01:45:24.734 --> 01:45:27.654
| doubt even Zero thinks like that.

01:45:27.862 --> 01:45:32.408
If he did, that would mean
we're being used as pawns, too.

01:45:32.617 --> 01:45:34.202
But that's impossible.

01:45:34.410 --> 01:45:37.497
His anger against Britannia is genuine.

01:45:37.705 --> 01:45:41.751
| think a person who knows anger
also knows what sadness is like.

01:45:46.130 --> 01:45:47.757
Calling A.S.E.E.C. head trailer.

01:45:47.966 --> 01:45:50.844
Zero sighted. Proceeding with capture.

01:45:53.137 --> 01:45:58.017
C-Can that be... The girl from
the capsule in Shinjuku?!

01:45:58.226 --> 01:46:01.437
Stop! You mustn't harm this man!

01:46:03.857 --> 01:46:07.527
Wait! What are you doing?!
That's a Knightmare you're challenging!

01:46:07.735 --> 01:46:09.863
| can't afford to let you die.

01:46:10.071 --> 01:46:12.490
It'll be indirect contact,
but it's still worth a try.

01:46:30.425 --> 01:46:31.426
Father...

01:46:31.634 --> 01:46:35.388
This is impossible. You should be dead...

01:46:38.975 --> 01:46:41.311
Hey! Don't tell me you're
giving that pilot Geass?!

01:46:41.519 --> 01:46:43.813
I'm just feeding him a shock image.

01:46:44.022 --> 01:46:45.982
| don't know what he's seeing, though.

01:46:46.190 --> 01:46:48.151
Anyway, use this chance to get away!

01:46:48.359 --> 01:46:51.779
Are you kidding?
Not while I owe you a debt--

01:46:53.156 --> 01:46:54.741
No, not now!

01:47:05.835 --> 01:47:08.671
What? This isn't what I saw before.

01:47:16.721 --> 01:47:17.305
What is this?

01:47:17.513 --> 01:47:19.599
St-Stop it!

01:47:19.807 --> 01:47:22.268
Stay... out... of my... mind!

01:47:22.477 --> 01:47:25.855
Stop it... Why?

01:47:28.733 --> 01:47:31.986
You're... opening me...

01:47:42.413 --> 01:47:45.375
It was all I could do!

01:48:00.807 --> 01:48:01.808
What was all that just now?!

01:48:02.016 --> 01:48:03.685
Idiot! Escape while you have the chance!

01:48:05.687 --> 01:48:06.771
C.C.!

01:48:08.064 --> 01:48:10.066
Hurry... and run!

01:48:12.902 --> 01:48:14.654
Your Highness! I'm coming now!

01:48:14.862 --> 01:48:17.365
Guilford, relay this message to all units:

01:48:17.573 --> 01:48:19.492
"Prepare to retreat."

01:48:19.701 --> 01:48:23.037
There's no reason to waste
the lives of any more soldiers.

01:48:23.246 --> 01:48:27.166
Maintain current battle status
and slowly fall back.

01:48:28.167 --> 01:48:32.171
We have to face facts. We've lost this one.

01:48:36.009 --> 01:48:40.680
You see? It's all Britannia can do
just to take on the Liberation Front!

01:48:40.888 --> 01:48:44.517
Well, they definitely gave us
the chance we needed to escape...

01:48:44.726 --> 01:48:48.813
Hey, where's Zero? I can't raise his Burai.

01:48:49.022 --> 01:48:51.190
You don't think he's been captured, do you?

01:48:54.652 --> 01:48:58.322
Is this girl really not human?

01:48:58.531 --> 01:49:00.867
The speed her wounds are
healing at isn't normal.

01:49:01.075 --> 01:49:03.828
She was definitely shot in the head
back in Shinjuku, too...

01:49:04.037 --> 01:49:06.289
Clovis was experimenting on her privately,

01:49:06.497 --> 01:49:08.624
so she must not be related to Britannia...

01:49:08.833 --> 01:49:10.460
Her vital signs are the same as a human's.

01:49:10.668 --> 01:49:12.837
I'll analyze this blood sample later,

01:49:13.046 --> 01:49:15.214
but I should get photos of her wounds, too.

01:49:20.011 --> 01:49:21.095
What?

01:49:27.477 --> 01:49:31.230
You finally called me by my name.

01:49:36.986 --> 01:49:40.073
So, in the end, Zero remains at large.

01:49:40.281 --> 01:49:44.994
The J.L.F. set up a defensive line,
so I assume he slipped past it.

01:49:45.203 --> 01:49:48.915
It's distasteful how he always uses
something as a shield to hide behind.

01:49:49.123 --> 01:49:50.792
And what about Kururugi?

01:49:51.000 --> 01:49:52.043
He's been recovered.

01:49:52.251 --> 01:49:54.837
They had to wait for his energy filler
to run out and immobilize him,

01:49:55.046 --> 01:49:56.464
so it took some time.

01:49:56.672 --> 01:49:59.342
Had to wait? Was there
a problem with his machine?

01:49:59.550 --> 01:50:03.429
Possibly. It appears he lost control of it.

01:50:03.638 --> 01:50:06.474
That's an uncharacteristic failure
for my brother's forces.

01:50:10.144 --> 01:50:12.980
| removed the shrapnel
and cleaned the wound.

01:50:13.189 --> 01:50:14.524
That was unnecessary.

01:50:14.732 --> 01:50:15.942
So it would seem.

01:50:16.150 --> 01:50:18.945
That's why there was
no point in your saving me.

01:50:19.153 --> 01:50:22.573
Your pride always gets in the way
at the most inopportune moments.

01:50:24.659 --> 01:50:26.953
Thanks to it, I learned something interesting.

01:50:30.998 --> 01:50:32.917
It's your name, isn't it?

01:50:33.126 --> 01:50:36.295
Eavesdropping is a nasty habit.

01:50:36.504 --> 01:50:39.966
A nice name, wouldn't you say?
Much more human than "C.C."

01:50:40.174 --> 01:50:43.803
Oh, how ridiculous.
Like I need to be more human.

01:50:44.846 --> 01:50:48.141
After all, I... I...

01:50:49.684 --> 01:50:52.228
I've forgotten... Everything.

01:50:52.436 --> 01:50:53.855
All that I knew.

01:50:54.856 --> 01:50:59.443
What use have I for a name now?
What use... for a name?!

01:51:04.824 --> 01:51:07.451
Since this is a good opportunity,
I'll say this now.

01:51:07.660 --> 01:51:10.872
Er... You saved me earlier.

01:51:11.080 --> 01:51:15.835
As you have before.
And you gave me the Geass...

01:51:16.043 --> 01:51:17.128
And so...

01:51:18.754 --> 01:51:20.339
I'm only going to say this once.

01:51:23.050 --> 01:51:24.260
Thank you.

01:51:26.470 --> 01:51:29.348
No one's ever thanked me before.

01:51:30.725 --> 01:51:33.686
Well then, can you show your thanks to me?

01:51:34.729 --> 01:51:37.315
Call me by it, like you did before.

01:51:37.523 --> 01:51:40.318
Hmm? Oh, that name?

01:51:40.526 --> 01:51:45.156
Just this once. Like you treasure it,
with tenderness in your heart.

01:51:47.450 --> 01:51:48.951
| suppose, if I must.

01:51:58.711 --> 01:51:59.670
Satisfied?

01:51:59.879 --> 01:52:02.298
Wrong. It was all wrong.

01:52:02.506 --> 01:52:06.093
Not tender enough.
There was no honesty or sympathy in it.

01:52:06.302 --> 01:52:10.348
You pronounced it strangely,
and most importantly, it lacked warmth.

01:52:10.556 --> 01:52:11.933
You're a picky girl.

01:52:12.141 --> 01:52:15.394
Of course. I am C.C., after all.

01:52:25.947 --> 01:52:27.156
Another soldier?!

01:52:27.365 --> 01:52:30.534
It just shows how much
our forces have fallen apart.

01:52:30.743 --> 01:52:33.621
I'm not Orange...

01:52:33.829 --> 01:52:35.998
Zero!

01:52:43.881 --> 01:52:45.549
Looks like our ride's here.

01:52:46.676 --> 01:52:50.805
Zero! Are you okay?
The other members went on ahead...

01:52:51.013 --> 01:52:52.723
Who's that?!

01:52:52.932 --> 01:52:54.517
You needn't worry.

01:52:54.725 --> 01:52:57.270
She's a very important friend of mine.

01:52:57.478 --> 01:52:58.562
Huh?

01:53:07.530 --> 01:53:10.116
The Japan Liberation Front
has been wiped out.

01:53:10.324 --> 01:53:14.036
Which of Cornelia's units was it?
To think they didn't leave a single survivor...

01:53:14.245 --> 01:53:18.249
Wait! He may be on the run,
but Tohdoh is still in good shape!

01:53:18.457 --> 01:53:21.961
But I hear he's even lost the Burai Customs.

01:53:22.169 --> 01:53:24.005
At this point, hope is...

01:53:24.213 --> 01:53:26.632
There is still hope.

01:53:26.841 --> 01:53:30.094
The Black Knights?
You've been an admirer of Zero

01:53:30.303 --> 01:53:34.807
since he rescued Suzaku Kururugi,
to the point of sending him a Guren Mk-II.

01:53:36.642 --> 01:53:41.147
The Japan Liberation Front was nearly
wiped out by your operation, Viceroy.

01:53:41.355 --> 01:53:44.400
One by one, we're capturing the remaining
members who are still on the run.

01:53:44.608 --> 01:53:45.818
Are you being sarcastic?

01:53:46.027 --> 01:53:48.404
We have to reorganize
our forces after that fiasco!

01:53:48.612 --> 01:53:50.114
Oh, no! That wasn't my intention!

01:53:50.323 --> 01:53:53.492
| believe a flawed occupation policy
was pursued from the start.

01:53:53.701 --> 01:53:57.830
Why have Area Eleven's subways
and mining railways been ignored?

01:53:58.039 --> 01:53:59.332
In the ghettos, no one is
managing family registries

01:53:59.540 --> 01:54:01.500
or clarifying property ownership,

01:54:01.709 --> 01:54:04.378
leaving them breeding grounds
for anti-government activity!

01:54:04.587 --> 01:54:09.008
Well, the subways stretch around
practically the entire country.

01:54:09.216 --> 01:54:11.552
We couldn't budget for all the tunnels
outside of the settlement to be filled...

01:54:11.761 --> 01:54:15.306
Even knowing they'd become the terrorists'
main bases and escape routes?!

01:54:19.018 --> 01:54:23.230
The student named "Lelouch"
should be around here somewhere.

01:54:24.482 --> 01:54:26.484
I'd like that document, please.

01:54:26.692 --> 01:54:28.944
Who do you think
you're pointing that gun at?

01:54:29.153 --> 01:54:35.159
| decided joining Zero would be more
interesting than joining the Purebloods.

01:54:35.368 --> 01:54:38.537
And you call yourself a Britannian, TV man?!

01:54:44.335 --> 01:54:48.839
"Chinese Federation Consulate General"

01:54:53.886 --> 01:54:57.306
Are you the "Black Knights"?

01:54:57.515 --> 01:55:00.851
Yes. And you're Dr. Rakshata from
the Indian military district, correct?

01:55:01.060 --> 01:55:03.396
Which one of you is using the Guren Mk-II?

01:55:03.604 --> 01:55:04.438
That's me.

01:55:04.647 --> 01:55:08.526
| hear you've been getting
pretty good data for us!

01:55:08.734 --> 01:55:11.904
Here's a protection suit as my thanks.

01:55:12.113 --> 01:55:16.951
Also, we'll be cooperating with you
until India gains independence,

01:55:17.159 --> 01:55:18.494
so let's be friends.

01:55:28.838 --> 01:55:32.049
So, now we find out whether
Kyoto will accept an organization

01:55:32.258 --> 01:55:34.635
whose leader wears a mask.

01:55:34.844 --> 01:55:37.805
There are also rumors
that Zero isn't Japanese.

01:55:38.013 --> 01:55:40.558
No use worrying about that now.

01:55:40.766 --> 01:55:45.354
Zero, you hide your face even in my presence?

01:55:45.563 --> 01:55:47.231
| have my reasons.

01:55:47.440 --> 01:55:51.026
But I will make an exception for you,
Lord Kirihara, because I owe you a debt.

01:55:51.235 --> 01:55:52.611
A debt?

01:55:53.612 --> 01:55:57.867
Yes, for your assistance to my sister.

01:55:58.075 --> 01:55:59.201
You'
re...!

01:55:59.410 --> 01:56:00.911
| am grateful.

01:56:03.122 --> 01:56:08.169
How far do your path
and Japan's path overlap?

01:56:08.377 --> 01:56:10.671
| want to lay my foundation here,

01:56:10.880 --> 01:56:13.674
in this place without Britannian influence.

01:56:13.883 --> 01:56:15.259
Very well.

01:56:15.468 --> 01:56:16.302
Ohgi.

01:56:16.510 --> 01:56:17.428
Y-Yes?!

01:56:17.636 --> 01:56:22.516
Your worries were correct.
Zero is not Japanese.

01:56:22.725 --> 01:56:26.312
However, he is without
a doubt Britannia's enemy.

01:56:26.520 --> 01:56:30.649
Follow Zero. That is Kyoto's will.

01:56:30.858 --> 01:56:32.151
Understood, sir.

01:56:32.359 --> 01:56:33.444
Will that be all?

01:56:33.652 --> 01:56:35.237
Thank you.

01:56:35.446 --> 01:56:38.491
And please give my regards
to Kaguya Sumeragi,

01:56:38.699 --> 01:56:40.576
who provided us with the Guren Mk-II.

01:56:41.702 --> 01:56:45.039
Naoto... it turns out that Zero isn't Japanese.

01:56:45.247 --> 01:56:49.210
But that's okay, right?
It's not like we're Japanese nationalists.

01:56:52.588 --> 01:56:53.881
Are you all right?!

01:56:56.467 --> 01:56:59.136
Speak to me! Hey! C'mon!

01:57:00.721 --> 01:57:01.555
You're alive!

01:57:01.764 --> 01:57:04.391
You... Zero...

01:57:23.202 --> 01:57:24.745
You're awake?

01:57:24.954 --> 01:57:26.497
Yes...

01:57:26.705 --> 01:57:29.833
Why were you collapsed in that place?

01:57:30.042 --> 01:57:30.960
What's your name?

01:57:31.168 --> 01:57:33.003
My name...

01:57:33.212 --> 01:57:37.174
What is my name...?

01:57:37.383 --> 01:57:39.552
Don't tell me you've lost your memory?

01:57:39.760 --> 01:57:41.887
What about Zero?! When I found you--

01:57:42.096 --> 01:57:43.305
Who's Zero?

01:57:44.431 --> 01:57:48.894
What the hell am I doing?!
| practically betray him, and now this?!

01:57:49.103 --> 01:57:50.813
But I don't know!

01:57:51.897 --> 01:57:53.065
Anything...

01:57:53.274 --> 01:57:59.863
I'm sorry! Um, I was able to undress you
with my eyes closed, but dressing you...

01:58:00.072 --> 01:58:04.159
But I turned up the heater,
so I figured you'd be all right.

01:58:04.368 --> 01:58:06.287
Thank goodness.

01:58:06.495 --> 01:58:09.456
At the very least, it looks like
| was picked up by a good man.

01:58:09.665 --> 01:58:10.958
Huh?!

01:58:12.418 --> 01:58:14.295
Huh? That's so weird...

01:58:14.503 --> 01:58:16.880
Lulu disappeared again!

01:58:17.089 --> 01:58:18.716
Hey, you there!

01:58:18.924 --> 01:58:21.260
It's not safe for you to be here alone.

01:58:21.468 --> 01:58:23.304
You hurry on back to your nice house.

01:58:23.512 --> 01:58:24.346
R-Right...

01:58:24.555 --> 01:58:26.640
Yeah, go home! Damn Brit!

01:58:26.849 --> 01:58:28.976
Come on, don't scare her so much.

01:58:29.184 --> 01:58:30.269
Heh, my bad.

01:58:30.477 --> 01:58:33.981
We won't lose while we've
got the Black Knights!

01:58:34.189 --> 01:58:41.905
D The future we dream of so fondly... )

01:58:42.114 --> 01:58:56.337
D ...is nothing more than
a boundless land to run in )

01:58:56.545 --> 01:59:05.387
> Hear us, O clouds, O wind )

01:59:05.596 --> 01:59:16.273
J» That wish belongs to our friends and to us )

01:59:16.482 --> 01:59:25.449
